5,'Looks good.  It is noticeably pinkish though compared to all of the other oil rubbed bronze in the house. The shower hose could be longer like 84 inches for my needs so I\'ll just get a shower arm extension for the handheld.<br /><br />Others have complained about the plate scratching the shower arm during installation.  It will if you install the arm first and then slide the plate on the long way.  Here\'s a hint, unscrew your old shower arm and make note of how far the plate was on the old one.  Then, push this new plate on to the new arm starting at the end that will be installed in the wall up to the same distance OR less.  THEN screw in the new arm.  You\'ll never see the scratches that are created when installing the plate because they\'ll be behind the wall.<br /><br />This was a replacement for an older shower kit I had and I found that the wall pole on this new one was too long for the holes that were already drilled.  So rather than drilling new holes, I used a hacksaw to cut the length of the new pole and it now fits fine.  You have to unscrew the pole from one of the wall adapters, the other is just a press fit.',B000UI7Y10,AFXIVLT6OT6X5URJDAF2P5BEITZA
