5,'I purchased this after giving up on traditional deodorant in an effort to eliminate toxins in our lives.  I had been using coconut oil and cornstarch for a few weeks, but decided I needed a real one since summer is around the corner.  And I have been blown away by this kind!  Yes its a bar, like soap.  I hold it on my armpit for a few seconds then swipe a few times, or more, depending on my plans.  I was instantly amazed.  NO WHITE BALLS!  I\'ve had those my whole life, even with \'invisible\' ones.  And then, after copious outdoor activities, in the sun for hours, I felt clean!  I did get a little damp, but NOT STINKY.  I even had my hubby sniff up close and personal and he said he barely smelled anything.  I am sold and now buying it for everyone I know.  P.S. I also LOVE the Ethique shampoo & conditioner bars and dog shampoo bar!!  >> Ethique customer for life!!&lt;&lt;',B07TN3W1KX,AHAI4LYOA5TQYCZQIDXKLKFYPD3A
3,'Pros: Arrived promptly and package securely.<br />Cons: Uncomfortable to wear, no instructions included.<br /><br />Purchased in July 2016, to help with small bunion. I found the toe straightener to be a bonus. It took me a few minutes to figure out how to wear it, I had to refer back to Amazon and look at the photo to figure it out. I wore it for several days before calling it quits. I didn\'t notice any significant improvement with my bunion, but when I removed the corrector, it kept my toe straight; temporarily that is. I wore it with my sneakers, which made it more uncomfortable. I found wearing under my socks while I slept was the most comfortable. When I removed the Tea Armor Corrector in the mornings, it felt like I still had the corrector on. I didn\'t have any adverse reactions. The corrector is made of a soft silicon type material. I don\'t know how long you\'re suppose to wear it, when or how to wear it for best use, since it arrived with no further instructions.<br /><br />Overall, my experience with the Tea Armor - 2 piece Premium Bunion Corrector was neutral, perhaps just a tad more positive than negative. I probably won\'t purchase again simply because the discomfort is too much to bear everyday. I didn\'t see any significant improvements but since I received the Tea Armor 2 Piece Bunion Corrector at a discount price, in exchange for an honest review, I didn\'t lose as much, as oppose to paying full price. I do believe the $9.99 asking price is reasonable. My sister said she wants to try them and see if it works. Her bunions are more pronounced than mine. If she has a different opinion than mine, I\'ll update this review.<br /><br />Seller: Ordered with no problem from seller. It was shipped promptly, arrived in tact, in two business days and was packaged securely in a large envelope.',B01E9WI0SS,AH2LBTO2DOKWJ3XHS6Y763OMAFCQ
