5,'When I moved, I had the opportunity to start with a new polycart that didn\'t yet reek of rotting garbage. I was advised to use these bags all the time, as they\'d prevent the accumulation of debris and water in the bottom of the cart, which is kept outside only partially-covered by eaves. They do the job very well, though I use an extremely large rubber band to anchor the bags to the can and prevent slipping. It\'s best to free the bag from the band before setting out the cart, but if forgotten it seems that the bag simply stays in the can--which it does occasionally even if the band is removed. While not essential to the use of the polycart, not having a foul-smelling and vermin/insect-attracting garbage can is certainly an improvement both for myself and my neighbors.',B00OY28D0O,AFF35TFGKAUNFVT4YVFCRNKM54JA
