5,'Ohhh yes I quite like these. Made the switch from shower gel to bar soap a couple years ago, and was using a plastic loofah-like soap pouch at first. Those took forever to suds up, and they’re still plastic. Not awesome.<br />In an effort to reduce my own personal plastic use, I tried these, expecting a sandpaper experience because my previous understanding of “sisal” is the stiff pointy rope that comes on cat scratchers. Friends, these literally feel like cotton out of the box. They soften up nicely in the shower also, just give it a minute under the water and you get a gorgeous rich lather and don’t have to worry about your soap slipping everywhere! Also, the four pack comes in one single box, they are not wrapped in plastic, so the goal of reducing plastic waste is actually achieved here. The only complaint I can think of is that I use up my soap slightly faster than in the thicker plastic pouches. But this may result in me getting one extra bar of soap a year, not a huge deal. Overall these are absolutely worth the purchase.',B07THJSBH1,AEYGAOO6OZLWFGMK4CBSE2IW7MQQ
