4,'I have no idea what this should cost, so I can\'t speak to whether it\'s overpriced, and I got mine in exchange for a review. That said, $17 feels expensive for what this is.<br /><br />It\'s nice to play with, and it softens as you use it. I found it moderately but not immensely helpful with an injured finger and hand.<br /><br />In spite of claims that it\'s non-oily, you can see that it arrived at least a little oily. After a couple uses it all worked either into the putty or out onto my hands, so I don\'t have any issues with oiliness now.<br /><br />Because I needed to work one finger and part of my hand, I pulled off smaller chunks to work with and would put them back with the main putty once I finished. It pulls apart with a satisfying snap, and it works back together into the main glob without too much fuss.<br /><br />I got this for an injury, but it has also helped with hand and wrist cramps, and it\'s a pretty enjoyable fidget toy.<br /><br />Overall I\'m satisfied with this product, even if I had to work out the oil and I feel like this has to be a little overpriced.',B09Z5X31LZ,AFMSOWVKU6SJH3VRC3UM24DHQZPQ
