5,'The only downside to this curler is that it’s hard to clean the clamp part. Other than that it’s an amazing curler. I dont imagine needing more than 3 settings. I use it every single day. I have rather long lashes that do not stay curled and this is the only type of curler that works for them. I look like I have had them permed or extended with this curler. Big fan.<br /><br />My routine:<br /><br />Pre-curl lightly just at the lash line. I use very minimal mascara after I do my eyeshadow. I then do my eyebrows. By the time those are done, my lashes are ready to be curled. The curler works best after dry mascara. I don’t tend to use the clamp part because I don’t like cleaning it, but it’s helpful for removing clumps and tangles before they get set in place by the mascara. The best way to use it is (after it heats up and the little dot changes color) roll it heating element towards your eyelid so your lashes are going up at a 90 degree angle and then let the lash fall on the curler as you lift the curler up and away from the lash line.<br /><br />Pro tip:<br />Waiting for dry mascara helps so much in avoiding mascara on your lids.',B08WZ2RPJW,AEXZ27HKNTL63IHYBIRPI7653HWA
