3,'UPDATE (4/21/20): After trying this product out for a few weeks now, honestly it was decent at first, but has become more of a hassle. It keeps falling off your nose and doesn\'t 100\% fix one\'s snoring. This is unfortunate because I was excited thinking I found the one sole, cheap product to at least help my case. It just might not be for me but maybe for someone else it will have better consecutive results.<br /><br />I am the guy and part of the population who snores like a train! I despise sleepovers for this reason and it honestly is a bother not only to others but to my physical and mental health.<br /><br />I purchased these just to give a try as it is key inexpensive. The product overall comes with 4 sets in cases and itself is a small rubber nasal piece that has magnets attached to clip together. I tried them on for a few nights and wanted a good idea of what I was getting myself into. My family members have said they haven’t heard me snore too much since using them! That’s awesome! They of course said it comes and goes so it wasn’t always 100\% effective. However, this might have been the case because this thing consistently kept coming off in the middle of my sleep. So I would have to search for it on my bed then put it back on. To prevent it from taking if you just have to readjust the way you put it on.<br /><br />It’s good for the price and can do the trick for some people. I wouldn’t say it’s for everyone though especially if you are a mouthbreather. This device only opens up the nareway passage to provide for air to go through and open your nasal serum to the lungs. Can’t hurt to try because if you don’t like it then just return it and get your money back!',B085HY8BZ3,AHEQ23SWCMRDURP27426GD7F6F6A
