5,'I love the sunflower pattern by Van Gogh! I have been using these microfiber cloths for at least 4 years already. They all come in a plastic packaging but then are individually packaged in a paper holder that I keep.<br /><br />They are great for keeping around in different spots of the apartment or different bags so in a pinch there is always one. I also like giving them away as gifts - the paper packaging helps with presentation and portability.<br /><br />I have washed them in the washing machine and hang dry. They are very well made and anything else is inferior.<br /><br />I even used them to make microfiber masks during COVID and I am pretty sure they work well because it was very hard to breathe in them - it makes N95 masks seem like a breath of fresh air. The material is so thick I had a very difficult time stitching in the straps.<br /><br />These are not your average microfiber cloths. They are very good quality and the only reason I buy more is because I give them away or keep finding more uses for them.',B08SBFHVVF,AGQLYLJK7H2ALE672THV5QGXXY5A
