5,'After trying several different kinds (many which felt flimsy or more like netting) I found these glorious FLUSHABLE diaper liners!  Flushable, durable, and definitely not flimsy, almost like a shop towel for diapers, lol.  Some people may say they are &#34;too rough&#34; but my son has pretty bad eczema and these don\'t irritate him at all.  Best part, is even when he has a big #2, the liner holds up and saves my cloth diaper from a huge mess.  Everything flushes neatly down the toilet.  Our house was built in 1911, and we have never had any issues with flushing, backing up, or anything of the sort, but we do live in a town so we are on a city sewer system.  I have used these for almost 2 years with no issues.  Worth every penny.<br /><br />*Also, we use BumGenius All-in-One and pocket diapers (not gDiapers...sorry gDiapers, but I do love your liners!)...these liners are nice and long, so when he was smaller, I folded the liners a bit in the back for extra lining, and as he got bigger they fit inside the diapers even better.  Now I still fold a little bit in the back so that after he\'s gone #2 theres a little more in the back to fold over the poo so I hardly have to touch anything, just wrap it up in the liner and flush!  Seriously, these are the best.  I don\'t normally review things, but these are too good not to review.',B01FJORVIA,AFJLZEOLOQAEZ6QO5SMFRO4QEFZQ
