4,'This hair remover machine - or eyebrow machine as I like to call it - is pretty nice.  The instructions say you \"switch the power up\" to turn on - but you just press the button - it is pretty simple.  The first time I turned it on it did turn on but the light did not - then I just tightened the top and the light works fine.<br />I found it very easy to use - it has like pinpoint accuracy and I did not feel like I was going to shave my actual eyebrows off or anything.  My eyebrows are super fine so I wanted to test it on courser hair so I tried a small patch on my leg - and it took those hairs right out too.<br />Personally I think it is a bit loud for what it is - it almost sounds like it is rattling - that is why I knocked a star off.  The only other one I can compare it to is this old one I have that almost looks like a razor - but that one is very quiet.  Otherwise I am not sure how they work industrywide.  Again - the way the head is set up - it really sounds a bit rattley.  It could just be me - as it is not too bad.  Plus it comes with a little brush to help clean it - and as a Bonus it came with two FREE eyebrow tools - a spoolie and then a brush/comb - so that is nice.  They are nothing spectacular but they are included - so again - nice!<br />If you found my review helpful, why not click the \"helpful\" button.  Thanks!',B08CRSZ6TF,AFGCJIO7DNVCCZPG4KVMKKXVPJLQ
