3,'Yes, you will look ridiculous wearing these.  However, if you suffer from severe motion sickness/vertigo, you won\'t mind.<br /><br />I\'ve been hospitalized more than once due to vertigo.  Of course, motion sickness is a common occurrence for me as well.  I used to be a gamer, but now looking at a moving screen makes me instantly sick.<br /><br />After my last hospitalization, I purchased these.  They help with working on a computer when scrolling, and help significantly when looking at my phone.  They aren\'t a miracle cure, the motion sickness doesn\'t go away, but it lessens it more effectively than OTC medication.<br /><br />Unfortunately, they seem to be designed for someone with a much smaller head than I.  I wear XL size baseball hats, and these glasses don\'t reach from my ears to my nose without stretching.  The part of the glasses that sit on my nose has ZERO padding, it is hard, pointed plastic.  As a result, it becomes painful after 10+ minutes of wearing.  It leaves deep, painful imprints.  A soft rubber coating or longer temple/earpieces would improve this product significantly.  I\'m currently trying out a few ideas to see if I can fix it myself.',B093D1MBLW,AFW4PY7KV3OHGBN46ORGCQVSG2FA
5,'These are really comfy and cancel out the noise perfectly.  As you twist them backwards, the spirals enclose and noise becomes silence! I’ve slept better since wearing these ear buds. They even stay in my ears all night and don’t need many adjustments throughout the night. 👍🏽',B07HRCRTBG,AHHORV4V4GRUBBZRECSONDUUFYOA
