1,'I had Lifestation for 4 years and did not need it.  One day I fell and hit the button, I lay on the floor bleeding and had to listen to the device tell me to push the button again if this was in error.  Then I got a machine telling me to hold for a representative.  I held and held.  Then I dialed 911 on my phone and just before the paramedics arrived someone answered.  They were impossible to understand, as the reception was poor.  A day or two later I called to express my concern for the service.  I talked to two people that were nice and very understanding, however they were not a supervisor.  The supervisor called me and had not sympathy or understanding at all.  She spent the time telling me that I could change the device and upgrade.  No way I was going to upgrade.  I told her that it was impossible for me to understand the rep because of interference.  She then then said that in my area the reception was poor.  I live in an area where everything else works just fine.  I would like to know why after 4 years they didn\'t tell me that the reception was poor.  I was paying them for good service and reception.  If you value your life and limb, do not under any circumstances use Lifestation',B07G9MTFX8,AGGJ7KJO3JXZRVQ43EU3PJACRINQ
