1,'I tried both the DownBeats and Etymotic ER20, both of which were actually PAINFUL to me.  The DownBeats are so short they were very hard to remove.  Some little pieces to these also, and they kind of fell apart easier than I am comfortable with.  I would hope those little pieces would not be able to come off, since they face toward the inside of the ear canal, but they fell apart in my case, and I noticed one review on Amazon where they did fall inside someone\'s ear, and they had to be removed by a medic.<br /><br />The Etymotic were so long I would not think I could sleep with them, even if they were comfortable.<br /><br />I did find some plugs that work, as The LiveMus!c HearSafe Ear Plugs are very comfortable.  They definitely cut the sound level.  They go in easy, stay in, and are pretty easy to remove.  The end of the plug is short enough to not interfere with hats, pillows... but long enough to grasp and remove.  I can sleep in them very comfortably.  The LiveMus!c plugs also come with 2 different sets of dB reduction levels, for a total of 4 plugs, an easily removable connecting string, and waterproof case.<br /><br />I suspect I have small ear canals, as I prefer the softer and smaller poly foam disposable plugs rather than the standard, and seem to be sensitive to plugs that other people have no issues with.',B00A3Z44RM,AEXZXHWR2LJWAVZPSIVXNBHDNUMA
