2,'I use these straps to keep my mouth shut so I don\'t drool and/or bite my tongue and prevent dry mouth. They are not a speck of help for snoring.<br /><br />This version has velcro and is thick, bulky, hot & scratchy.  The shape doesn\'t help keep it in place.  There are better jaw supports without Velcro and with a double-strap system that goes on top and behind the head for stability.  This one is better in my opinion: [[ASIN:B00JOQIP3K PCS 500# Snore Eliminator PRO Adjustable Chin Strap Support]]  The very best is at mysnoringsolution.com.  They originally sold for a few bucks.  Now it is stupid expensive.  Such is greed.[[ASIN:B01CH4X0D0 My Snoring Solution Anti Snoring Jaw Strap W Free Sleep Program. Stop Snoring No Sleep Apnea Masks]]<br /><br />Update:<br /><br />By far the best is \'My snoring solution\' found here.  It\'s stupid expensive, but it works.  The vendor sells it for $80 elsewhere on the web. [[ASIN:B07C6XWCX1 My Snoring Solution Anti Snoring Stop Snoring Jaw Strap Chin Supporter (Large)]]  Beware, there are imitators.  Look at this photo:  No velcro.  The support is light and soft with elastic straps between a front and back band that allow me to fit it around my ears and not over them.  That is the key to comfort.<br /> https://www.amazon.com/My-Snoring-Solution-Strap-Supporter/dp/B07C6XWCX1/ref=sr_1_5_a_it?ie=UTF8&qid=1531171459&sr=8-5&keywords=my\%2Bsnoring\%2Bsolution&th=1<br /><br />There is a very close \'my snoring solution\' imitation on ebay for about two bucks.  I like it because it is light, comfy and cheap.',B01BV74HHC,AGUKXDSEENGWNYABIO7CLDHH6J3Q
