4,'I am a 6\'2&#34; 205# male. i ordered 3 styles of camp ben products. CAMP BEN (TM) LARGE Padded Posture Corrector was difficult and frustrating to get on and very hard to reach under my arms to adjust, i took off the padded shoulder portions and it was somewhat easier to get on.<br /><br />The Figure 8 Clavicle was very uncomfortable under the arms, i think due to the extra thickness of the straps and it dug into my arms and chest much more than the padded unit. it\'s labor day weekend and am still expecting one more unit to test.<br /><br />The 3rd unit worked best for me, it was the CAMP BEN Posture Corrector Clavicle Brace. The vertical strap on the back allows you to reposition the underarm straps depending on your size. For me I lowered it to the very bottom. I wore it all day yesterday and again today. Today I think I found an easier way to get it on and adjust it. I attached the hook end of the velcro strap end only about a 1/2&#34; on the loop portion, then when I put it on I could reach under my arms and easily detach the straps and pull them tighter. it you attach all of the hook portion it is much more difficult to detach when reaching under your arms. this method would probably work with all 3 units.',B01EIS61HU,AFM4YWD37CLVTT4CS62OQYIWUDCQ
