5,'I was desperate.  My work demands long hours of sit-down time.  I would get so sore I had to stop working for several hours.  I had tried all sorts of pads, cushions, and even the fancy new ergonomic mesh chairs.  Nothing seemed to help.  I began to develop sore points on the bottom.  Then one day the Purple commercial popped up on my computer screen, complete with the &#34;egg test&#34; and Goldilocks.  I was interested.  Checked out the site.  Did not believe their claims, but I was willing to try anything.  Received the chair pad in record time.  opened it that night after a long sore day at my desk.  I thought that the rubbery, sticky, purple mess was just a scam.  Placed it in the cover as instructed, and sat down.  Much to my surprise, even after already being sore from working all day, I detected some relief.  The following day, using the Purple pad at the outset, any residual discomfort resolved and I was able to complete my tasks without the pain!  What a relief.  As I write this, I am sitting on their pad.  I plan to look at their other products now. The pads are a little pricey but I would have paid more for the relief that I have received.  I got the 2 inch pad, but the 1 inch might have worked as well.  Oh, by the way, I decided not to do the egg test....no need to.',B01CKMP34S,AHKYUEYE5GMDKNA2Y5BY2LBJNPCQ
