5,'After hip replacement surgery, I was left with a leg that is about 1&#34; longer than the other.  Although I got an orthodic heel from a professional, I felt like I needed a &#34;back up&#34; heel.....until next spring, when I will have the other hip replacement done.<br />These fit perfectly, although, they are too high to be used in a regular slip-on shoe.  I use one, whenever I wear boots;  since it\'s the winter now, I am using a heel life from this set EVERYDAY.<br />I love that it comes with layered parts, that can be removed if one inch is too much of a lift. It can be adjusted in 1/4 inch increments.  It\'s very cushioned and comfortable too.',B00TZH7H6E,AFYER5QIDHTJXV5W77QLCOCGTXGA
5,'I have used a nail grinder on my four dogs’ nails for over 10 years. I had always used the ones that had little sandpaper attachments. They’re fine, but wear down over time.<br /><br />When the time came for another grinder I decided on this one because the price was right, and because I wanted to try a grinder with metal attachments.<br /><br />This grinder fits my hand easily, and I like that it’s cordless. It’s quiet, which is great because 2 of my dogs are very resistant to nail time. The metal heads work as well as sandpaper and I suspect they will hold up better over time. Hopefully the battery will. That’s what usually prompts me to get a new one. So far, so good!',B08CR3HHHN,AG3E3PBK6UWKY6O3ECILNR42MZXA
