2,'My dad had a pair just like these that he bought at a airport 50 years ago. Unfortunately he forgot to take them out of his pockets when he went to court to pay a ticket and they were taken. He tried to find them again but unfortunately the company, that was based out of france, went out of business/ bought out. The craftsmans ship of those clippers was flawless. They clipped just as good as they day he bought them 50 years ago. I was thrilled when I found these. Upon opening them I was a little disappointed. While they cut great the craftsmanship is poor. They do not sit flush down, they will hook on anything in a pocket. There was a crease in the metal. When opened it goes to the side. These would be great pocket clippers if it wasnt for the sloppy craftsmanship. Clippers cut great and file works great too, craftsmanship poor.',B075LDDFV7,AHH5ARRBWPYZIULAHLWURW2GAYFA
