5,'Got this Iron Chelate along with the EI based NPK + CSM+B Dry fert package from his website and thats all you need to fertilize any planted aquarium. comes in a nice package with a zip lock feature. however i just convert all of my dry ferts to  tupperware for easier opening. the dry ferts are very easy to administer with measuring spoons. I think he even has a chart on his site on how much to use a day. but I use 1/16 tsp 3 times per week in the morning on tuesday, thursday and friday. the other fertilizers are a whole different story and are AWESOME and last forever, like a couple years. but this is about the Iron Chelate.<br /><br />I see so many people doing low maintenance tanks and complaining about dying plants and not growing plants, just get some dry fertilizers. you will not regret it. you just measure them out and put them straight into the tank. so easy. just make sure to do your water changes every week to keep the fertilizer levels from building up too much. If I miss a water change on a Sunday, I just skip the fertilizers for one week until i can get a change in. no biggie.<br /><br />This is good stuff to add to your fertilizers. I don\'t think it is completely necessary but it will really bring out the red in your plants. especially if your on the edge of being high light. below shows a before and after picture of using the fertilizers. Maybe about 4 months apart and Im running about 2 watts per gallon for my lighting. thats not very high light.<br /><br />hope this helps! Will update with pictures as the tank progresses.',B0143DZVVW,AHORLHQHXGHOLZ3LCZA3ZT4P2XTQ
