4,'I ordered recently from this posting showing six silver sponges and I received six silver sponges, no gold. I prefer the silver ones, too. I will give these five stars as soon as I find out from the manufacturer whether they contain an added &#34;antibacterial&#34; or whether the &#34;antibacterial&#34; quality is in the nature of the polyester fibre. I avoid anything labeled &#34;antibacterial&#34;. These sponges are longer lasting than the other very similar ones, which are very flat. I think the quality that people like in these sponges is that they are denser. The sponge inside the curly covering is made of a finer and thicker foam. So they feel more substantial yet they\'re very easy to squeeze. Like mom said, if you don\'t leave any sponge lying in the sink, if you use dish soap liberally on it, if you rinse it out and let it dry between uses, it will last a long time. That said, even with only one of us taking care of them, they do last longer than the other silver ones and are more pleasant to use.',B00RY30C8Q,AH4NBKEBQUPRFFBP2YCFMWQZMWHA
