3,'Over all it\'s ok, not the best but definitely not the worst. I have to put my meds through a jtube so they have to be crushed first and I was looking for something that was compact and easy for on the go. This grinder is definitely compact but it\'s lid doesn\'t hold very well so if you want to use the pill holder section be prepared to dig in the bottom of your bag for them later. It isn\'t quick to grind either, if you only have 1 or 2 small pills to crush it\'s fine but if you have any more than that or anything larger than a tylenol be prepared to twist the thing for several minutes and occasionally have to pull something out break it in half and then try again because the teeth don\'t want to catch on larger items. Even with these issues it\'s still better than the other compact pill crushers I\'ve tried and as long as I put it in a zip lock bag before it goes in my bag the lid popping open isn\'t an issue (without the ziplock you will get residue from the meds you crush in your bag)',B08NTCV6WJ,AHNP6XTIHND7WZ6O7FFNY23WSQVA
5,'I like these pipe cleaners. Just turn on the hot water and let it run for a minute, turn off the faucet and pop one of these in. As rasy as that. If you must, they will easily snap in two. They foam just a little, but the bubbles stay inside the pipe. The scent is not strong, simply use 1 pipe cleaner per drain to take away unpleasnt odors or partial blockages. I live in a homemade home, so things are a bit irregular, but not my drains!',B07P7FH4JN,AHHRFMJL7W6EEAZ53V5Y26M757ZA
