3,'I can\'t review it based on its claim to lower cholesterol yet because I just started taking it.  As far as the powder goes, and being able to \'hide\' it in foods, I would say it takes a little thought.  I\'ve found that a half scoop in a large cup of coffee works, provided I first put just a little coffee in and stir it hard with a fork until all the bumps are gone; then I add the rest of the hot coffee.  I also hide it in yogurt, but again give it some hard stirring with a fork to get all the lumps dissolved - about a half scoop per yogurt is all you can safely hide.  For health benefits I also add a big scoop of oat bran which gives the yogurt a nutty texture and helps hide the nutrim even better.  Getting a second scoop in per day has been a challenge, but do-able I believe.  If this works to lower me 40 points, it will be worth it.  If not, it will have been an expensive challenge for nothing.  I\'ll try to remember to come back in January 2018 after my next blood test and update this review with my results.',B007RZ3A94,AGY72YGAJPJX7GLOPTBAZASAYOGQ
