5,'I used this filter blaster for the first time today on the cartridge filters of my robotic pool cleaner. It was a last attempt before spending around $130 for a set of new filters.<br />All I can say is “WOW!!”<br />I followed the instructions on the bottle to a ‘T.’<br />First I hosed off all loose debris, made sure the cartridges are soaked well with water, then sprayed them with the blaster, and let them sit for 5 minutes. After that, I hosed them off thoroughly (important, because if you don’t you could end up having foam issues with your pool), and right in front of my eyes the cartridges turned from blackish gray to a shade of off-white. They don’t look like new, because they simply aren’t, but they look nice and clean again, and have given me the opportunity to wait on buying a set of new ones.<br />The company recommends to let filter cartridges air dry if you have the option, because it gives the filter material an opportunity to “fluff,” which increases filter efficiency.<br />I am very satisfied with this product. From now on this will be my go-to filter cleaner.<br />Just try it out, and you will find that this filter blaster is worth every penny you paid for it.<br />Just look at the before and after pictures I posted. That alone should convince you of the amazing quality of this product. Way to go Applied Biochemists!!',B079HB9B53,AECLT4PCV2S2MPTRQXTR5B2ZHGDQ
