5,'I\'m doing a 14 day \"test\" to adjust insulin doses, as I wait for my own Freestyle Libre to arrive (got approval paperwork last week).  I am always skeptical of adhesives (either allergic, or they fall off).  While the adhesive seems good, I wanted a \'bump guard\' type of thing, and this is very handy. I don\'t feel it \'squeezing\' my arm, and it hasn\'t moved, and stays right over the adhesive, leaving the sensor open so the reader has no problem working with it.  I\'m glad I ordered a second green one, and just sent for 2 pink ones.',B07D9R7HSV,AEXP4AULLRFINXRFJ3FXQDFYYOWA
5,'I was skeptical, but figured I\'d give it a try.  Turns out it works FAR better than alcohol, although I\'m pretty sure the ingredients of the first bottle are just alcohol and d-limonene (orange oil), which makes sense because d-limonene is a fantastic and safe cleaner.  With the first bottle, you just put a few drops on the surface, wait about 30 seconds, and wipe the old thermal paste off.  This stuff eats the thermal paste away so there\'s really no scrubbing.  I do this twice just to make sure everything is off, but that\'s just me.  It\'s somewhat expensive, but it does work really well, although next time I need to clean a heatsink and CPU I\'m going to mix some d-limonene in with some alcohol and see if it works the same.  If so, I\'ll just start making my own concoction.',B001JYQ9TM,AE4HY7N6EJDHOYX4MEJ623SBBQ7Q
