5,'[UPDATED REVIEW]<br /><br />We discovered a couple of shortfalls with two of the eight masks we purchased across two separate orders through Amazon.<br /><br />At first we purchased four individual black adjustable masks, finding them to be light, comfortable to wear and featuring a very practical keeper strap.<br /><br />After one wear and wash, however, thread on the keeper strap on one of the black masks was found to be fraying, the material bundling, and it looked like it was about to fall apart.<br /><br />The white adjustables just arrived in the last day or so, and upon opening the package today we found one of the four to be missing a loop through which the keeper strap is to pass.  It looks like it\'s just a little tab of material, and it doesn\'t serve any purpose.  The mask is useless without it.<br /><br />I reached out to the Seller to request replacements for each of these two defective items.  While the response time could be better, Buttonsmith stepped it up, sending to us replacements for the masks that were not up to standard.<br /><br />Things happen. A great measure is how a company or individual responds when said things happen. I\'m more than pleased to share with you my experience that Buttonsmith did right by us.<br /><br />I am a survivor of COVID-19, battling the disease for 36 days.  There were times during the first couple of weeks in particular I thought I was going home.  As a Post-COVID19 Long-hauler, I\'m still battling symptoms.<br /><br />It\'s not political. It\'s not about control.  Do our part. Show you care.  Mask up.  Buy this mask. Buy plenty of these masks.  And wear \'em. (We\'ve since purchased another set of four white adjustables.)',B08B7RRTF4,AG4TO2HZKDEBIMHUGOGB46LBKLDQ
5,'I have tried so many masks that were either too tightly pulling on my ears, or fit okay but were cheaply thin with weak stitching. These adjustable masks are game changing. Their quality, fit amazing and don’t break the bank. All while being made in the USA. 10/10 highly recommended. Admittedly I had to return the non adjustable mask due to being too tight but that’s a me problem. The adjustable makes are the way to go.',B08B7RRTF4,AFTOQIC5FHDJ4OIX7Y36PIS3FK2A
