5,'Left side of photo is clean and right side is dirty.<br /><br />My travertine floors are cleaned every week but the dirt is too much with our dogs and daily traffic to be cleaned with just the average vacuum and mop.<br /><br />I have an oreck orbiter which is a MUST for everyone who is OCD, owns expensive flooring, and/or owns animals who live a better lifestyle than you.  I too bought the green bristled brush for the oreck and sprayed this cleaner with a lawn and garden sprayer onto the floor and then proceeded to clean with the orbiter.  Because I forgot or rather blocked it from my memory, my husband claimed he had a 10:30AM tee time.  After a few homicidal thoughts and counting back from 10, I did a really quick swipe of the piece of floor I just sprayed.  I then had five minutes of wait time for the cleaner to sit which I used to stare at said husband with a “who the hell invented golf because I am going to make it a sole goal to haunt this person” look.  After a quick wipe up and a quick dry, I assumed I would take up the chore again when my golfing husband gets back from the 19th hole.  I really did not expect anything because I felt I did a very quick, poor job on the one spot.  After about 4 hours of dry time, I could not believe it.  The travetine and grout look great.  This will be my go to when I need the deep clean but not in the mood to use the gorilla diamond polishing pads.  The diamond pads are great to use to get the shine back on travertine floors.<br /><br />Husband is still playing golf now so I will report back if anything changes or if he doesn’t come home and need a new husband.',B01M8GC1TO,AGNB44SKOFLMDL4BWEPA35SGIDNA
