5,'I was tired of the mesh loofah balls that I have been using for years. My skin is more sensitive and I have a rare skin condition that causes me to feel uncomfortable very easy. I also have arthritis and neurological conditions that make it challenging to hold a regular wash cloth. So, I ordered a variety of products to see which one I prefer best. After trying different sponges and loofahs, I ordered more of these. Here’s why:<br />Pros…1. Even though it’s silicone, the long bristles allow the body wash to lather and it holds the soap as you move to different parts of your body. Note that I tried a different silicone loofah sponge with shorter bristles and it did not lather up the same. Since the long bristles hold the soap, I use less soap than I did with the mesh loofah balls.<br />2. The bristles are very soft on my skin and don’t irritate it at all. The flip side is good to use when I have an area of skin that needs a little more elbow grease to clean. It’s actually good to remove the remnants of barrier cream and other medications, dry skin, etc.<br />3. These are so easy to keep clean. After my shower, I just put them on the 3rd rack of my dishwasher. It has a sanitizer cycle. The bristles don’t get completely dry, so I just let them finish drying on the drying rack. With the mesh loofah balls, I had to put in a mesh bag after each use, wash with my laundry, and hang to dry. With these, I know they are completely clean.<br />Cons…1 They don’t have a loop to hang up on a hook or to hold on your hand. It would make it easier to hold on to if there was a strap on the back to hold it on. It would also be easier to hang dry if there was a string to hold it up. I have cute decorative soap dishes that I put it on to dry in the shower, so I make it work.',B092HZ3W4D,AGRSBALYBDIWVDVCO6PTI4GKP7BQ
1,'I bought this comb hoping to make a stylized bun with the elastic design over the center. It wouldn\'t hold for even 10 minutes. Giving up on that idea (figuring that perhaps the bun was too thick) I opted for a french twist, which is significantly less thick. It worked about the same as the bun (lifespan of 10-15 minutes).<br /><br />I\'m guessing (hoping) that this comb works better for people with shoulder length or shorter hair. If your hair goes past your shoulders, don\'t bother!',B007SP0GD6,AEU76O52STFGSKH342ZJZOOQXS7A
5,'For someone who has worn contacts for 20 years, since the age of 12- ClearCare was a game changer.  When using normal solution I had issues- eye infections, red eye, weeping eyes . Since exclusively using Clear Care I haven’t had any issues.  It prolongs the life of my monthly contacts. My ONLY complaint is that I wish the two packs came with two “cases.”  If you are someone who doesn’t take your contacts out until late and may not get a full 5-6 hours in the clearcare case- I’d recommend investing in a bottle of saline to “rinse” off well or your eyes will sting.',B004O2A29E,AHBQCIOT4JDHIT5CMKFXMLKBQ2EA
