1,'And not in the way it was supposed to. I have very visible pores on my nose, and I usually clean them out weekly with a pore strip. Well after 15 years of buying pore strips, I decided to try one of these.<br /><br />So I did my usual routine of showering and washing my face with hot water and a facial cleanser. Then when I got out of the shower, I attempted to use this on my nose. Instead of removing anything, it just left me with a red welt on my nose. I tried different levels of suction, different nozzle tips - not a single one extracted anything out of my nose, but left me with several painful red splotches.<br /><br />So it\'s back to pore strips, which managed to once again pull out all the gunk that this thing missed.',B083TKLH45,AHGB4WCB5B3RUETM2GV3I7DOZHPQ
