5,'I\'ve been using this remedy for leg cramps for about 5 years. It is amazing, and I always make sure I have a bottle ready for me. I keep mine in the kitchen, so I can quickly make it myself (or even have my kids or husband rush to the rescue).<br /><br />I usually mix it with about 1-2 ounces of water, although I have also dumped it into whatever drink was quickly available, when I couldn\'t get to water quickly. This remedy is on my travel checklist, as leg cramps are common for me when I am sleeping away from home. I try to always keep a full bottle in the cupboard, so I never run out. I am glad to see this special deal for multiple bottles.<br /><br />I am plaqued with terrifying leg cramps, unlike the &#34;charlie horse&#34; leg cramps I used to get as a teenager. They often wake me from sleep, but can also strike me when I am awake. My toes will seize up, and start curling backward, or there will be a burning cramp that rushes up the front of my calf and inside of my thigh. I have to jump up immediately, or they will paralyze me in my seat. There are times when I literally can not get my foot off the floor, to get to the kitchen for my &#34;leg cramp stuff&#34; (that\'s what my family calls it... LOL!)<br /><br />It might be due to my varicose veins, but nothing my doctors have suggested has worked. I gave an empty bottle to the doctor who treats my varicose veins, and now he stocks it on his shelves at his office! Amazing stuff. My mother also relies on it, as it works for her similar issues.<br /><br />The one thing I will warn you about, is the taste. It does have a yucky taste (like vinegar), and especially when you get down near the bottom of the bottle. Make sure you shake the bottle before use, and just don\'t pay attention to those strange floaty shadows in the bottle, as you are using the last of the formula.<br />I have tried drinking this straight from the bottle, but because I also suffer from peptic ulcers, it burned and made me double over in pain (while waiting for relief from the cramps). I am 41 years old and at a healthy weight.',B00CZDMLZM,AEUIBGPHDZOQYPLVHD4CNAVJBEGQ
5,'First off – be prepared to not want to go anywhere for a while. This was the first vibrator that I bought to be used internally rather than for clitoral stimulation. You can get rabbits in all shapes and sizes, even different colors, to suit your taste and experience level. I went for the classic, partly because it had won awards and partly because the other reviews spoke well of it (and there is a reason why). The multiple speeds available on the \'ears\' can be adjusted to suit your preference and the rubber is flexible and soft enough so that you can adjust pressure and position to hit the sweet spot. The shaft is thick, but not too thick and the pearls rotate to stimulate the opening of the vaggg (the lower 1/3 of the vagggg is where 90\% nerve endings are) in a delightfully decadent way. There are three speeds for both the shaft rotation and the ears, so you can combine them in a multitude of ways. The shaft can also rotate in both directions, so experimentation to find the perfect combination is nothing less than exquisite fun. There are models that come with remotes but I have found that, with either a partner or by yourself, the fun is in the playing and I like the hands-on approach. If you are able to climax quickly, you\'ll love the ability to slow it down and tease yourself (or have someone do it for you).If you are someone who can sometimes take a while to reach the peak, this is definitely for you. The multiple sensations and stimulation will allow you to relax and concentrate on nothing but the feelings and your fantasies. You\'ll find that even when you have reached your destination, you may want to keep on riding.<br /><br /> I received this at a discounted price for my unbiased review',B01BF75QE6,AGKFFQUDXL7ZM35RAEQTUYZW274A
