5,'I tell everyone about these!  They are a miracle as far as I am concerned. I have had sciatica for two years.  I’ve had PT, spinal steroid injections, lost weight, TENS therapy, more PT- nothing worked.<br /><br />I was “better” in that I was not dragging my leg but I was in no way pain free. I was taking scheduled ibuprofen 4 times a day and Tylenol in between just to make it through work. I found these at Family Dollar of all places and thought I’d try them. I started out pretty much maxed out on them. I wore 3 the first day one on my back and two on my leg. I do tend to have a mark where a bandaid is and this is the same sort of material so I can tell where one has been for a few days. Rotate your sites.<br /><br />By day 3, I was wearing 2 a day and had bought all I could find so I ordered from here.  I gradually went to 1 a day and at about 3 weeks i noticed i wasn’t putting one on at all. Y’all, I don’t hurt anymore. Not even a twinge. I can sleep in any position-not just with my leg bent (sciatica people know what I mean).<br /><br />I’m at the gym, I can squat, do pelvic lifts with no spasms or cramping. I keep a few at home now and one in my gym bag and in my desk at work just in case but honestly, it is just for peace of mind. If you ever had sciatica you know I’m terrified of it coming back.<br /><br />Buy these you won’t regret it.<br /><br />Oh!  And yes you can take a shower and wear all day. They stick. Not like those from Aspercreme that are like a gel thing that roll up at the edges and stick to your clothes.',B072W9JWLC,AHV57TTES7JWKEBQHIGC4CGENJWQ
5,'I have the 3 pack of clear gel squishy shoe inserts.<br /><br />They were a good addition to a new pair of 3 inch heels that just arrived. There was a slight learning curve (for me) in applying this style of inserts.<br /><br />Getting the main gel insert (below the toes) at the right position took me 3 tries on the first shoe and 2 tries on the second. There is additional material to support the toes so it is essential to get the position correct.<br />The back piece was also quite tricky for me as my shoe has an elastic piece at the back of heel. A couple tries to get that placed.<br /><br />Tall heels are way more comfy. Now I just need more practice wearing them before the next event!<br /><br />ASRAM Heel Cushion Inserts,Reusable Anti-Slip Shoe Pads,Heel Grips for Loose Shoe,Shoe Insoles and Metatarsal Pads for Women,Heel Blister Prevention.(12Pack)',B0B45W838G,AFDD3EZSP42AJS3RNTGKGNYE24MQ
