5,'I was recently diagnosed with osteopenia, and started to take a calcium supplement with D3, but after doing more research, I felt I needed to add magnesium as well.  I started taking Kappa Nutrition Magnesium, and I\'m always grateful to not experience any negative effects such as stomach upset.<br /><br />This product is Made in USA using globally sourced ingredients, had a tamper resistant safety seal, and has a best by date of 05/2024.  I take 2 capsules and they\'re easy to swallow, plus, I have not had any stomach upset.  I\'ve found that since I started taking this magnesium product, I haven\'t had any muscle cramps, and I had been getting frequent cramps is my hands, calves, and even thigh muscles, and believe me, the thigh muscle spasms are excruciatingly painful.  I\'m also sleeping better, and find that I\'m falling asleep faster, often while I\'m still sitting up in bed reading.  I have IBS-C, and have had some improvement in my constipation since taking this product.<br /><br />I\'m very pleased with the benefits I\'m getting so far from this product, and I feel that the current price of $15.99 for a 60 day supply for me is a reasonable price, and I will continue to take Kappa Nutrition Magnesium.',B09XQZ7F3J,AEJVFDEWF7VCSCEZ5CZTKYVTJY3A
