3,'When checking Amazon for finger file product options earlier this year, I learned many reviewers have discovered that the Revlon file offered today is nothing like the quality that has been available for years.  They no longer have a lifetime guarantee, the flip side is not a \'finishing\' grit and they wear out and need replacing in short order.  After reading such positive reviews for the glass files, I ordered one (mirror).  I was pleased with the smooth edge it gave the nails, but in short order it snapped, despite taking exceptional care when using and storing it.  I didn\'t replace it, as I was having a difficult time using it comfortably due to the file\'s thickness and the fat tip couldn\'t get under the nail.  So, reluctantly, I reordered the Revlon file.<br />It\'s amazing to me that with all the advancements in technology and medicine, there doesn\'t appear to be a company that can design an effective finger nail file ! Too bad .....',B009W1RL2I,AFFJVJXB5Q3L2NVHWHKIFGWENRCQ
