4,'I typically use a flat iron to straighten my hair- tried this brush because the price was right to experiment. I like this tool- it seems to work quicker than the iron, at lower temps (200 vs 400 degrees), and I experience no tugging/pulling. I do not know how a thick, super curly hair would manage with this- the &#34;bristles&#34; are not especially easy to comb. They are tipped so as not to burn scalp (good feature) but it does not grab the hair very easy- kind of skims over the outer layer not getting thru to the scalp.  I scoop my hair under with the brush and use my other palm to press my hair through- its a 2 handed operation and works much better (than if I wasn\'t) holding my hair against the hot bristles..... and because its tipped no burns! Use the temp lock feature- the +\\- buttons are in the exact spot (as a righty) and i press them accidentally when brushing. I\'ve used this brush more than my iron since I received it. If the bristles were more brush like than I would give it 5 stars.',B01M0LB5D4,AGTXPLHRKWKSYHBJ726OOZT6BBTA
