5,'I have morgellons (self diagnosed because John’s Hopkins acted like they had no idea what was wrong with me and wanted to make me a life-long pharmaceutical customer - prescribed me 1200 mg of gabapentin daily.) I lost my health insurance (as a single mother making $36k before taxes So I was no longer eligible for medical assistance.) I forced myself to work despite the pain, fatigue and brain fog. I was taking other natural remedies and came across the Samsara line in June. I have spent $480 from June to September. I started taking the TICK RECOVERY, then saw the TICK IMMUNE SUPPORT (capsules) and gave that a try. I went to order more but they have been sold out for 5 weeks, so it’s back to the TICK RECOVERY POWDER, not a fan of the taste.  I came across the BIO-FILM and decided to pair that which the TICK RECOVERY.<br />MORGELLONS has 3 of the 5 bacteria as LYMES. I advocated for a specific blood test after my LYMES test came back negative. Sure enough - I had the 3 bacteria.<br />When I started back in June I had a very bad herxing period, which I was happy about because I knew it was working. Since I have maintained a consistent dosage even thru switching from the powder to the capsules back to the powder - I haven’t experienced the herxing symptoms as bad. Now that I am adding the BIO-FILM in to my regimen I will update and let you know. I plan on taking the TICK RECOVERY 2x per day and BIO-FILM 1x (eventually 2x) per day. I am praying this speeds recovery.<br />I appreciate the Samsara line, and I am grateful that it seems to be working, but it’s very expensive to maintain. I don’t notice a decrease in pain of my joints. I can tell that it’s working because my skin irritations are starting to heal. I understand they need to profit, but they need to understand that their clientele is ill! Basically this regimen could cost $100/month. Paying taxes, being a single mom, with no assistance , no help, and working while ill is financially overwhelming. I watch ppl receiving food stamps, HUD, cash assistance and all other welfare benefits  be so wasteful and honestly it is very frustrating knowing I give 1/3 of my pay to support that.',B01LYG4MMR,AEEZQJVVQO32SRT2H6J7AJ3577VQ
