5,'If you trim the foam inserts about half their height for the 50-60\% of the foam insert (lower side), to avoid bending eyelashes that could otherwise start scratching your cornea once bent, you can use this as a night eye mask with moist foam inserts, since the Tranquil eyes mask they sell is too small and ruins your eyelashes.  This is the only mask on the internet I found that works well without ruining eyelashes if you trim foam inserts since it\'s big enough to avoid that.  :)  It will help prevent dry eyes.  While I don\'t use this as cold or warm compress, it may work for that, but I tried to use it once and it seemed to not release heat.  But warm compresses are overrated, just a warm shower and meibomian massage then is more than enough, or wearing sealed safety glasses to keep eyelids warmer and oils flowing is enough.  The far more important thing is to keep eyes wet at night, which this thing can do, even though not all use it for this purpose.  :)  I would not use this for cold compress since you want to barely touch eyelids and have full control, like wearing a glove and moving it, to avoid ocular damage from too much cold, which can be as bad as too much heat too.  Keep your eyes happy and moist.  :) For warm compress you can just warm them a little in warm water and use them as such, since mild heat may be better and do less damage;  recall that heat increases oxidative stress and can damage vitreous gel and cornea, if overdone, so it\'s best to focus on gentler heat and other preventive measures of meibum regeneration, than extreme heat.  :)  The 2 billion dollar computers are not fixed with warming or cooling them up, if that was so it would be easy.  It can be a costly 50 million dollar repair.  Same with eyes.  Think about an instrument, so expensive, does heating the whole of it fix it?  Our tech is not advanced enough to heat only the eyelids, it heats the whole eye which is bad.  Only Lipiflow avoids ocular heating, by heating only the eyelids with their meibum glands.  So, don\'t go to extremes of heating eyes, but a little eyelid warmth is good.  :)<br /><br /> Recall buying LacriPure saline eye drops (made for contacts-wearers, but anyone can use them) to keep eyes moist during daytime with minimal chemical toxicity, since it has water and salt only and 300 mOsm/L, the ideal osmolarity of our natural tears.  Saline often works fine when our eyes are not too \'tired and dried out\' :)  Make sure your foam inserts in Tranquil Eyes are not pressing on the center of your eyeball, since this will give you glaucoma in the long run.  Trim it in a perfect concave shape  (for the upper half only, not lower) maybe to embrace your eye perfectly allowing you to not touch the eyelashes, yet keep eyes closed.  I know this is hard, but at least, don\'t bend eyelashes and have some moisture there, get an amazon squirt bottle with purified water to wet them if they become dry in the middle of the night.  :)',B0764G69R4,AF52TO3MJUY2NHZT6EIEI2O3K3RA
4,'This is very comfortable. There is definitely a chemical smell that I hope will go away soon. The only issue I have is that the strap it came with does not seem to hold it in place no matter how tight I make it but that may be because of the design of my office chair.',B01CKMP19U,AGY3VFIFUGL2MM62HZFLE5HRHXDA
3,'Swift transaction but pricier than others',B009AW3CJK,AEZZL7523V4CPNVNL77ZWKZHJZBA
4,'I don\'t know why people were complaining about set up. I set my scale on a hard floor, and it took me all of 10 seconds to connect it, and then it told me to weigh myself. It was absolutely easy.<br /><br />The sleek design is so attractive! The bottom of the scale is covered in a bubble look and it really does look futuristic. This connected nicely to my Fitbit, and My Fitness Pal. Infact, I weighed myself, and it auto uploaded without me touching a button. So that was nice.<br /><br />I\'m really glad I invested the money for this scale. It seems to be accurate, seeing as how I was just weighed at the doctors office 1 week ago and have lost a few lbs off that number. Which I am trying to do. So as far as accuracy goes, this seems to be right on key.<br /><br />I need to keep it hidden from my kids though because it says not to be used by anyone under 10. And the look is just too tempting.<br /><br />The display is nice! It recognizes you by the account you set up and calls you by your initials. You can also set up multiple users. I am really happy with this purchase. ( So far :)<br /><br />UPDATE may 6 2014.  Got on the scale this morning and it read one weight.  Which I thought was impossible.  So I got back on.  It was 4 lbs down.  Huh?  Got on again... 2 lbs up.  Got on again.  1.2 lbs down.  This scale is messed up, and I am returning it.  I know my body fluctuates but not like this... And not in a 5 min time frame.  The scale integrates nicely with MFP, but make sure you watch it for inconsistencies. Mine is a white one.  And I originally really liked it.  However, I\'ve weighed myself only a handful of times since I got it, and it fluctuates like mad',B0077L8YFI,AG236DRG76LWHLRM2NELMLD3KRXA
