1,'This review is NOT for the Kailo patch, it is only for the purchase of additional adhesive.<br />They suck! They’re clearly expired. If you look closely in the photo, hopefully you can see there’s all these squiggles on it. The adhesive is not supposed to look like that. They don’t want to stick to the actual Kailo patch very well, but it’s near impossible to get the clear covering off the front of the adhesive to stick it to yourself. Once you do, it’s sticks on pretty well initially, but they slowly peel off. And you can Never reuse them again…for $25. That’s ridiculous. The original adhesive, I was able to reuse 5-6 times. I will re-purchase additional adhesives from the actual Kailo company.<br /><br />As for the actual patch, I find they work really really well. But not for all pain, like they clearly do nothing for my migraines… as I would practically have to stick them in my hair. But for my low back pain, they eliminate it but easily 80\%<br /><br />Edit… as if 5-10-23 The seller reached out to me & offered me a apology & full refund. I must say I’m quite impressed. I didn’t expect that. So 2 thumbs up for their customer service. Based on that, I will probably consider re-ordering the adhesives in the hopes I get a better batch. I personally really love the Kailo patch for my back pain. It really allows me to get things done. For reference… it’s the Facets & discs in my Lumbar area.',B07Y3D88K7,AE3DJBRFMZ5WP4DS7TFSFJCLFZLA
