1,'The product description is purposely confusing to make you think goody bags are included.  There are NO goody bags included, just the 20 balloons for $16.99.  The balloons also have a seriously strong, nose burning, chemical smell to them.  I have not tried to inflate them with helium yet, so I can\'t comment on the quality.  But I am sitting in a large ventilated room with these balloons and I can smell an odor coming off them that\'s burning my eyes and nose.  Therefore, I don\'t recommend these balloons.  I\'ve never opened a bag of balloons before that gave off any odor, much less such a strong chemical smell.<br /><br />Here is the confusing and misleading wording in the first paragraph of the product listing:  ■ You are about to buy a 20 Pack - Pro Blox Builder Miner Video Game Truck Birthday Party Balloons- Great Roblox Supplies Favors, Goody Loot Bags Decorations (Size 12\" - Big Ones)<br /><br />I\'m usually happy with my Amazon purchases, but not this time.  I hope this doesn\'t happen again.',B07C6KNC4X,AEVCOPK3XYM62VDFHKPGZOK3ANEQ
5,'I love Everlywell’s tests and I love that they partnered with the Natalist brand for this test. Like Everlywell’s other kits, this comes with everything you will need in Natalist’s sleek hunter green packaging. There’s a registration card, detailed instructions, a lab form, band aids, lancelets, alcohol prep pads, and gauze. The test card and everything else has your kit # on it so nothing can be mixed up. A prepaid return mailer is in the bottom of the box, too.<br /><br />What does this test for?<br />LH(Luteinizing Hormone)<br />FSH(Follicle Stimulating Hormone)<br />TSH(Thyroid Stimulating Hormone)<br />Estradiol<br />Testosterone<br />All key components that influence your female fertility.<br /><br />Also what I like about this test that differs from Everlywell’s own tests is the QR code you can scan on the back of the box. It takes you a Natalist webpage which gives you an in-depth look at what roles your hormones play in your fertility health and why it’s important to have them tested.<br /><br />2 tips: 1; if you’re squeamish about needles I would have your hubby, significant other, or bf help you with the lancelet. Just press down firmly(it’s spring loaded) and one use each. It doesn’t actually hurt I just have issues doing it to myself lol. It’s a small prick, as if you slipped when sewing, easier than having blood drawn by a mile.<br /><br />2nd tip; make sure you’re well HYDRATED before doing this. You don’t want to go through the process only to find out you don’t have enough blood for the test card. All the little circles must be full.<br /><br />I recommend this test for any woman who wants to check her reproductive health or is trying to conceive. Or if you suspect you have hormone imbalances, PCOS, or have a hard time getting in to get lab work done. These tests are easy, private, and reliable!',B0B2ZKV7JY,AG2L2V7VZCTSJXDAMHS2IQKGK4XQ
