5,'This helps my low back pain and pain with my hips.  I am a dental hygienist and I wish this pad came in different sizes.  I use it on my operatory stool and it is a little big.  I also wish it came with a sealed fabric cover.  I would like to be able to use my surface disinfectant spray on the cover.  It really helps with sore spots and my low back pain.',B01CKMP24E,AGDZBCT3OIG6EQWSWL7PCJWS5KKQ
5,'I ordered this cushion because I game a lot in long sessions. It\'s really easy to strap to a chair as it has a sort of &#34;harness&#34; in the back that uses four straps to attach to any chair. The material is very comfortable and it sinks just like you\'d expect any memory foam cushion to do. The curved design helps keep your back straight, which ultimately fixes your posture and back pain. After a few long gaming sessions, I found that my back hurt a lot less or just didn\'t hurt at all afterwards. The cushion is also very good for the car, my mother drives a lot so I let her borrow it for long trips and she says she loves it! I did receive this cushion for my review, however all my thoughts and opinions on the quality of the product are genuine. I\'d definitely recommend this to anyone that works on computers, drives a lot, or just sits down a lot of their day. Very comfortable and useful',B017UQ1MEO,AH3QGRIOFKI5S4XSJDPWJHFOE6PA
4,'The buttons and labels are large clear. It\'s great for Seniors and is easy to use. The built-in microphone is fixed and omnidirectional. It plays through any standard stereo (3-conductor) 3.5mm earphones or headset, though &#34;in-ear&#34; earphones are best. Avoid &#34;Open Air&#34; headphones since the sound coming out of them will cause feedback. Also, very high sensitivity (greater than 100db) earphones work best since the amplification is not tremendous. The user\'s own voice gets amplified, so you have to get used to that. They\'re much better than &#34;cheapies&#34;. It does have a &#34;tone control&#34; that can boost either high or low frequencies. But I find the limited total frequency range of the device limits the usefulness of this feature. It has another jack on the front that allows you to directly connect the stereo RCA jacks on the back of a TV to this device with the included long cable. Plugging it in turns off the microphone, though you can toggle it back on so that both are on if you want. Overall it\'s a very good device.',B008MBPXCE,AFSZLC5QGBBDN7GFZWXMVLQPRZJQ
5,'Solgar is a great company - been using them for decades.',B006IB84PS,AHTSK2W72ZTGO7YIKEGG7E774Z4Q
5,'They are exactly what my doctor wanted me to have for swelling in my legs.  They provide the graduated compression and aren\'t lunch lady tan or old man black.  They are well made at I believe they will last a long time.  Seriously, for the price you just can\'t go wrong.',B085J1WBGR,AH4NVB2A5QRMNVLUWVW6KX44BOPA
1,'I bought two pairs of these, paid the $30.00 &#34;shipping&#34; charge to Europe and was then presented with an additional charge of €32 from FedEX for two little pieces of soft plastic and I find them pretty much useless. AXIL stated &#34;The $30 covered shipping and this other invoice is for the taxes and duties which we have the customer cover&#34;, so it total, for two pairs, $79 + €32!<br /><br />The marketing blurb states &#34;comfortable hearing protection&#34; but getting them into my ears can take minutes and feeling the \'button\' to push is hit or miss. They are no good for sleeping with, as stated in the marketing blurb, as their profile is too high and I find them painful, so unless I sleep on my back or face I can\'t use them. Like most people, I sleep on my side. A very disappointing product and horrible purchasing experience. Never again. I returned to using wax or cotton wool, which I can get them in more quickly and out faster than it takes to find the \'button\' on this product which I binned. I found them a waste of money.',B01C94W2BY,AFP4ILIKNMJISKOZYPFGDT3HU3IQ
4,'Pros:<br />Much more affordable than Waterpik<br />Smaller footprint in my small bathroom.<br />Comes with a base that holds brush, brush head, and flosser  head<br />Replacement heads are comparable with original Waterpik replacement heads prices<br /><br />Cons<br />You need to provide your own wall plug -not a big deal for me because I had extras<br />If you\'re rushing and don\'t put the brush in the stand correctly, it won\'t charge.<br />If the battery is too low, it won\'t do the deep clean at the high speed.<br />I often hit the mode button when I meant to press the power button which means I have to scroll through the modes to get back to my preferred setting.<br />Replacement heads are cheaper than Waterpik but more expensive than off brand replacement heads.<br />Only 1 tip. Less tip variety than Waterpik. Doesn\'t have tongue scraper, Plaque Seeker, Pik Pocket, or Orthodontic tip.<br />Even and high speed, it\'s much weaker than the Waterpik on the low speed.<br /><br />I had a Waterpik Complete Care Water Flosser and Sonic Toothbrush, WP-900 since February 2016 because I was too lazy to floss. I wasn\'t good about using the water flosser. I mostly used the toothbrush because my dental hygienist said the water flosser was a good supplement, but shouldn\'t replace normal flossing. I really liked that brush even though it stopped holding a charge after a few years. My daughter needed a water flosser so I gave her mine, and I decided to get this combination. I almost bought a different brush because it was lavender instead of blue, but I bought this one because it came with a base that would house the brush, brush head, and flosser head.<br /><br />I haven\'t used the actual flosser yet. I\'ll update this review if I do. I bought this because I wanted the option to floss without having to buy another item.',B07TLKR8TZ,AGDCEL53TWR756PF3ZHFL4OV56FA
