3,'Honestly, not sure what I thought regarding the aromatherapy aspect, but since you just add it to the water it is hard to really say it operates any differently than any other humidifier.  As such, it works reasonably well and the changing colored lights are a nice addition.  However, as other reviewers have mentioned, even with the light changing feature off, turning on the humidifer engages a bright blue LED on the front.  You can turn it around or cover it up, but if you are very light sensitive and want to use it while sleeping, I would steer clear.  Also, the hole for filling it with water is pretty small, so cleaning it will not prove to be an easy task.  Overall, I would suggest a better (and larger) humidifer that you can scent with whatever oils you like just as well as this one.',B00L6Z34KG,AHXP6C5NWXEZ432C6ZVLFU2AKGEQ
1,'I use soft contacts and I have a very strong prescription (-9).<br /><br />I read the reviews and they seemed to be glowing, so I pulled the trigger. I was hoping to pick this up so I didn\'t have to clean my lenses by hand multiple times to get rid of any residue.<br /><br />After a week of use I realized that this not only takes longer to clean, but does a very poor job. The mechanical motion creates countless small bubbles that I had to get rid of and still left residue. I also made sure to completely clean out the canisters and replace the fluid to make sure the fluid was clean. There wasn\'t one time when I unloaded the contacts and didn\'t have to clean them by hand.<br /><br />This may be a useful product for hard lenses but I had to return it.',B001RDD2QI,AFIESJSD4MTLWWZSYEQFWKO2NGSQ
