4,'I tried a few brands of these over-the-counter 4\% lidocaine patches, the max concentration available w/out prescription, after knee replacement with normal postop pain. (None will completely remove all discomfort, so I don’t expect that.)<br />I was skeptical but wanted to decrease my opioid prescription ASAP. I felt better after a few hours but it wasn’t until 24 hours that I felt I could attribute it to more than wishful thinking. Fifteen days postop I am now adequately controlled with acetaminophen w/one dose of opioid at night and before PT.<br /> I liked this product because it is lighter-weight, adheres better, is thinner so more flexible, comes in a child-proof container, and is good for 12 hours, not just 8, so more convenient for morning and evening application. I use 2 at a time, one on each side of my patella where the most common TKR pain is. Be aware that  in one can there are 10 strips, meaning using 4/24 hour day means one can lasts  only 2 1/2 days, so plan accordingly.<br />Small complaint: the picture doesn’t accurately show this, but there’s far too much (big plastic can) packaging for the amount of product enclosed; no option for getting many more per can, so that’s a lot of plastic in the landfill. But needs must.',B08BSW498Y,AEL5SWZOTOPQEKJFM4Y4UBJBOVUA
5,'It is so quit that I forget its on. Glad it has a timed function so it will shut off when I want.  My  allergies seem to be doing much better after using this machine consistently for a couple months.',B09XJW5VPY,AFTQ72CDFFJWKMXK6PTRBGJITNCA
5,'These anti-blue Reader\'s are phenomenal! First of all, they are very clear, comfortable, fashion-forward, and stylish. I purchased 2 of the black pair. One for myself and another for my hubby, who either breaks most of the eyewear he purchases, or looses them. So far, so good. He hasn\'t broken or lost them! the hinge is made in a fashion, that\'s flexible, and won\'t easily break. Easy to put on or off. Has a great black pouch; which you can also use to wipe off fingerprints. I enjoy also the Trendy/ Nerdy oversized style of them. I don\'t have any dislikes about this purchase.<br /><br />Thanks Amazon,<br />Teri H.',B0842GNX9V,AHHTH7Z2PVU2RZZK5C2TKIBTBJRA
5,'I have only tried the hair static spray so far and it works great! I was having problems with my hair being really staticky in the winter, but after I got this spray and used it on my hairbrushes a couple of times a week - problem solved!',B018X66WDQ,AGJSCY7QKANUU4ASAYG6P2VZ3VNQ
3,'I own the Sonicare Water Flosser. I\'m guessing that\'s my baseline for this review. It\'s not perfect. If we could fuse the Sonicare with this Water Dental Flosser Oral Irrigator, it would be the perfect machine for the task at hand.<br />Now, let\'s discuss this Dental Flosser Oral Irrigator. It\'s rather large, standing almost a foot tall without the nozzle attached. About half is the water reservoir and the other half is the handle with the controls and digital display. There\'s 2 buttons, the top is the power and it starts the water flow. The bottom button toggles thru options and changes the water pressure. There\'s a hidden lid on the top that lifts up and allows you to store two nozzles. That is a nice bonus feature for storage or travel.<br /><br />The instructions are rather simple. Rotate the water reservoir a few degrees to remove it from the handle, fill with water and reattach to handle. Press the top button for power then press it again to start the water flow. This is the messy part. You should have the nozzle in your mouth or you\'re going to get wet. Once that water jet starts, it\'s shooting a lot of water. So, you have to just open your mouth and let it drain all over the handle and your hand. Not to worry, the MFG says it\'s rated IPX7, which means it can survive being fully submerged, so drool and water dripping on it shouldn\'t be an issue.<br />This thing is pretty powerful. It caused a part of my gum to bleed. That\'s not a criticism. I like to keep my dentist employed so I haven\'t flossed in 5 days, so I definitely need to resume the daily floss. Anyway, particles of the Greek salad I had for dinner littered the sink, so this flosser did its job very well.<br />\"So, Mister gross no floss guy, why only 3 stars?? It sounds like this water flosser did its job\"<br />Well, yes it does seem to floss very well. However, I believe some improvements are needed before you\'ll pry those remaining 2-stars from my wet drool and food particle covered hand. There needs to be a trigger or additional button to allow control of the water. Currently, you start the water and it comes out non-stop leading to the drooling mess. If you could control the water, you could control the drool. They could also preprogram the water to come out in bursts. I was initially impressed with the larger water tank, but it turns out that larger reservoir is needed due to the amount of water this thing spits out.<br /><br />In summary, it does floss well, but it is fairly messy from my experience. If I figure out a way to make it a little less wet, I\'ll definitely edit my review with my suggestions.',B0BD3J31NY,AHCC5N7Y5ZMFKG7G5ZARQLQPBM3Q
5,'It took some time to get here, well after Christmas. My Mom still likes it!!',B07CPQPP16,AE4PLKENFRJGFS4KDRJA2OCFSHSA
