5,'For flat metal keys this works great, over the years I\'ve gotten in the habit of carrying upwards of twenty plus keys mostly for the many types of locks on our farm equipment, buildings and field gates. This was damaging to the pockets and over time has caused significant wear on the metal keys.<br /><br />I put 11 of my plain metal keys mostly backup farm  vehicle keys and a large number of out building door, gate and  pad lock keys.  I have been carrying it for a couple of weeks now and it is working well protecting the keys and protecting my pocket.<br /><br />The weight hasn\'t changed, much, but the compact way the keys can fold up has had me starting to search my pockets or turn back to the farm equipment  thinking I\'d left a key ring in a key switch or lock.<br /><br />The above isn\'t a problem, just have to get use to the extra space and very different feel from the key  rings.<br /><br />I was worried about some of our pad locks in tight spots, but so far it has had no problems with locks in tight spots..',B07BMYW8XV,AFFFFDK36C4QOP6C4OOWCGBA46HA
