1,'When it arrived one side was all gooey from the thin rubber coating being dissolved by too much heat maybe. Then it was claimed to give out 2 HOURS of light for 1 MINUTE of cranking. So I gave it 2 minutes of cranking when it arrived, and got only a few SECONDS of VERY dim light. So tried for about 5 minutes with the same dismal results. Then cranked for some 20 minutes with no better luck. Total China junk, it\'s useless.<br /><br />The instructions state that the battery needs to be cranked/charged after every use and every 30 days. So this is probably old stock with dead batteries. And personally this defeats my intended purpose of having a crank powered flashlight to keep in my backpack so I wouldn\'t have to worry about forgetting to keep replacing flashlight batteries.',B000F3W2TO,AEMOLHADGEOVQWXJDO2Y2CKWMQMQ
