2,'The assembly was not easy. The fasteners that attach the back to the seat did not line up without effort. It took well over 1/2 hour to attach the arm rests to the steel frame because the bolts would not line up.  If studs and nuts were used it would be much easier to install the arms.  In order to recline the chair, a knob on either side of the chair must be loosened. It is possible that, over time, the  fasteners that attach the knobs will strip allowing the back of the chair to fall backwards unexpectedly.  One must get out of the chair to loosen the knobs to recline the back of the chair. The padding is adequate,  but not the most comfortable if one wishes to spend any amount of time in the chair.  The allen wrench(hex key) provided for installation of fasteners is inadequate.  A hex wrench with a much longer shaft  would make installation of fasteners easier.  If one is not experienced at assembly, one could have difficulty assembling this chair.  I assembled the chair by myself but it was not easy.  Another set of hands would make assembly much easier.',B07NC1M73C,AF4LEYS6OLBOBWLHXM3KMVGLZ36A
