1,'I washed, clayed, compounded, polished and wiped with isopropel alchol then applied this  via dry method. For starters It doesn\'t really make it that much glossier... It does make the car very smooth and that at least has lasted a couple weeks along with very good hydrophobic characteristics. But the down side is, it doesn\'t last, more then a couple weeks, the brake dust seams to accumulate more and is more noticeable. Also since it is pretty good at beading and repelling water, the contamination, dirt, dust etc in the water seams to be left behind and always dries in place when it rains. Which is fine because that happens naturally.. My issue is it isn\'t any easier to clean because of it. Once the dirt dried on it after it rains over night or something, it is very hard to remove along with the water spots.(doesn\'t protect like a ceramic coating) also you get a white film residue around door handles and other odd areas where water can sit and drip down.<br /> overall this is a good sealant to be reapplied every two weeks after a full wash and light polish<br /><br />I wanted to love this product cause I don\'t want to permanently ceramic coats my car but this product is kind of pointless cause it isn\'t an easy clean result like real ceramic coatings but it still acts like a ceramic coating so if you apply it, you can wax it or spray wax it or spray detail it cause... Dear god it will be streak city cause the paint does get sealed. But it just isn\'t a useful sealant.<br /><br />I want my car to be clean looking always so I constantly wash and spray wax it to keep it looking it\'s top and this doesn\'t help in that matter at all. The reason for a 1 star and not like a 3 star level is the price.... Was a waste I could have baught allot more better products then waste it on this',B07D3YJ3VJ,AHUREQEDGSWPVUPUL2MKYKZDQLFQ
