5,'I am a protein powder conniseure as well as partners in a supplement company that we make our own protein powder so I am extremely picky when it comes to make a smoothie or shake with anyone\'s protein powder.  I read up on the benefits of Collagen Whey and decided as I fight the wrinkles that I\'d rather put something natural in my body that helps with collagen than all these gimmick creams and serums you read about out there.  I pretty much ordered three different variations of Vital Proteins Collagens proteins and will be trying all 3 and reviewing them but so far making a Strawberry Banana Smoothie with this one TAKES THE CAKE!!!!<br />Recipe<br />1 cup unsweetened almond or coconut milk<br />1/4 cup creamy peanut butter<br />1/2 teaspoon vanilla<br />1 cup frozen strawberries<br />3/4 cup ice (if not using frozen bananas)<br />Blend all above, then add.....<br />2 scoops of Vital Proteins Banana, Cinnamon and Vanilla Collagen (add last to blender)<br />2 frozen bananas (or regular) I just like mine frozen-- if not frozen add ice<br />Finish Blending....Makes 2 full 8 ozs of smoothies',B01M7O1N30,AFQYPUGY2PMR3Z7RXK6WCPZ352EQ
