4,'The greatest value from this 2-in-1 sonic oral device is the water flosser. The waterpik is fairly efficient at cleaning between the gums. It is an added asset to have an attachable toothbrush head for travel but its performance is not as impressive as that of the water flosser. The overall performance is good enough as to exclude an additional sonic toothbrush for short time travel.<br /><br />A glass or cup from a hotel room can be filled with the tap water which is needed for the fluid stream through the thin suction cable. I found that a small children\'s cup of roughly 4-ounce liquid capacity is sufficient for throughly flossing the entire mouth. It is possible that a small paper or styrofoam cup may also be employed without it tipping over.<br /><br />I had some problems a few times in which there was no jet water stream from the pick. This was easily remediated by placing the thin suction tubing in the water cup, turning the center power button on, and sucking out the air until there is a flow of water.<br /><br />It is definitely a good asset if you don\'t mind the addition of the suction tube and the cup for its operation. Another plus is that it eliminates clutter because it is USB cable charged. Not a bad way to keep in your pocket ten--10 to thirty--30 dollars by holding back from the more popular brands such as Phillips and Sonicare.',B07RFFKHJX,AH2JUWZNRPVUK27WZCY2E6ABVPMQ
2,'Don\'t really work for me. Purchased to use at work; can still hear all the chatter.',B01KYBRN9A,AH2WHIMOD4Y2ZNPDXRTL2NRSVTEQ
5,'I mistakenly used Resolve to clean a stain on a wool rug and it left a horrible greenish brown stain on the rug. I thought it was ruined. I came across this stuff and put some in a bowl with warm water. I dipped a rag in the bowl and dabbed the stained spot on the rug and like magic it was gone the next day. I then spent the next month scouring that rug for stains and dabbing them out. I’m still dabbing to this day. So satisfying.',B08FBK151X,AGDOCH6IIIU57IT7MMP6RPGXUKVA
