5,'I use these straws with Take and Toss cups, and they work near perfectly together. These straws are a little bigger than is intended with the Take and Toss cups, but you can shove them in, and after the first time it\'s a firm fit.<br /><br />I like that these straws are a little more sturdy than you\'re run of the mill straws (or the ones that come with the Take and Toss cups), so that my toddler does not completely destroy them in his first couple minutes of using them. They actually survive well enough that I have some that are at least 9 months old. They just get used, washed and used again and generally keep going. It feels good to be reusing something this much. Every once in awhile he\'ll manage to chew one to death, but it\'s a rare occurrence.<br /><br />After they\'re stuck into a cup, they definitely are not coming out again. It\'s a dinky little piece of plastic, but it makes all the difference in the world. I like the multiple colors too. It\'s been helping me track how old the straws are.',B003L7O7FS,AEWB44EBLA7NU5GBQOGX2AIAN5QA
