5,'I got this mat a few days ago, and I am surprised about how sharp the lotus spikes are. I was a bit scared to try it at first to be honest - but I definitely had to since I bought it. Lol<br /><br />So what I did was I wore a very thin shirt and started lying down on it. You know, just to get a feel of what it is like first. Well, it is true that it was a little uncomfortable in the beginning. I was left with a large area of red across my back. But after a few days, I am now proud to say that using the mat without any fabric or clothes on is the best thing I\'ve ever done in my life. Yes, the spikes may look deep and intense but they are indeed bearable. You just have to relax, and don\'t move once you get in position. Also, you shouldn\'t worry about the redness on your skin after each time you use it. It will abate and always disappear. Well, for first timers, I would simply suggest to just get a feel of it first. Use it conservatively, as we all have differences when it comes to tolerance and sensitivity. Do some researches as well.<br /><br />Moving on... The first 5-10 minutes will definitely make you feel energized but longer than that, you will start feeling relaxed. For someone like me who always suffers from back and neck pain, this really works. Instant relief, I must say, when I got up. This acupressure mat is just so relaxing and revitalizing that I can feel the endorphins pumping throughout my entire body!<br /><br />I HIGHLY recommend this acupressure mat product! Even though I know there are other less expensive types of this mat in the market, I believe this one is the best! It has excellent quality for its price. The lotus spiles are firm and sturdy. It is well worth the money and I guarantee you will make it a part of your daily routine!<br /><br />I definitely have no regrets!!!',B07KF1LKR1,AH5MWVWI75F3JQHQJNRYNJ6EW2EA
