2,'KitchLife Reusable Bomboo paper towels 1 roll in Hot Pink. The roll is large. The “paper towel” itself is quite stiff and rough-textured to the touch. It is fairly absorbent and you can wring it out and go back in for more— the way brawny brand paper towels “look” on the commercials lol. These would be great for those with toddlers/many juice or liquid spills.<br /><br />Aside from that, their “reusability” depends on how far you’re willing to go. Personally, I don’t have the desire or time to rewash these. Nor do I think they would hold up in the washer. Not to mention, being a similar texture to laundry sheets, they’d probably pick up detergent and all the various fuzzies, dirt, hair, etc. No thanks!<br /><br />Thirdly, I felt good about getting these “eco-friendly” paper towels until I looked at the ingredients closely. It lists bamboo pulp, wood pulp, and PP(polypropylene plastic)! And the fact they felt it necessary to add “All specifications are subject to change without notice.” Yeahh, that’s a red flag for me. Go with another brand!',B0BPBNG5RF,AG2L2V7VZCTSJXDAMHS2IQKGK4XQ
