5,'This fish oil is amazing for many reasons. This review is for the liquid lemon version.<br /><br />Taste: To me, it tastes and smells exactly like fresh-squeezed lemon juice. Light texture, clean, very nice right off the spoon. Best when chilled.<br />Purity: Has a five-star rating for purity and potency with the IFOS. (Go to IFOS.com to check the listing).<br />Potency: One little teaspoonful has a whopping 1,600mg of omega-3, at 800 EPA and 500 DHA, plus 300mg of other omega-3s.<br />Vitamin E: Added for preserving the oil, and to counteract any loss that you might have from processing the omega-3s. Just 10IU, so not excessive.<br />Natural triglyceride form: Carlson\'s molecularly distills this oil for purity, but does not concentrate it, thus it is left in its natural form. Nordic Naturals does the same with its liquid omega-3 (not the Ultimate Omega version). It works.<br />All in all, the Finest in cost, quality, taste.<br /><br />Great value: Even at full retail price, this liquid is hands-down the most omega-3 for your money.',B001LF39S8,AHMMRIU6XJMUGPQT6G3OL4UQUJUA
