4,'It is an accurate and reliable daily weight scale. SO much more accurate than the digital because, being disabled, I need more time to get on the scale and balance my weight. This one allows me the time to do that. The digital scales I\'ve tried decided my weight prematurely and I can repeat the procedure 5 different times in a row with 5 different weights varying by 10+ pounds. This scale I just step on and balance my weight, get the reading, and then step off. So easy. The display can be slightly difficult to read in low light (especially with my eye floaters and cataracts) so that\'s the only reason I gave it 4 stars not 5. It wouldn\'t be a problem with someone who has good vision. This is a vastly improved version of the &#34;old fashion&#34; analog scales they used to make.',B00ZGULUSK,AE5YZN542EZPJVTMOTF3U3FR5WQA
