1,'Tandem just keeps shooting itself in the foot.  They cannot design (or seeming)  HIRE ANYBODY with a lick of design SENSE to design a pump case - that works.<br /><br />This one does not have any clipping ability, it only slides on, but that is a misnomer and it is actually a struggle to get it on clothing.  You will have to PRY the clip (at a HUGE effort) away from the back of the case or TEAR your clothing, to try and force it over any pocket edge or anything fatter like your pant\'s waist or a belt loop.  OH, but if you push it onto a T-shirt hem - it will fall RIGHT off, unlike the ones that CLIPPED ON.<br /><br />It is miserable to try and get the pump back out of, it once forced in.  You have to remember (carefully) or watch the video repeatedly to learn the \"secret\".<br /><br />I long for the light weight plastic ones with the actual spring clip, that popped apart into two halves,  that came in a myriad of colors, that were made about two years ago.  I could change them out in a heartbeat to go with any outfit, UNTIL...... Tandem stopped selling them.  Of course, any spring clip will wear out or break so they need to be replaced eventually.',B01NB16DW9,AFVDXM5T2JJEWL4TVPRGY7GUM5HA
