2,'First of all let me say that I have purchased and used another competing product that\'s only slightly more expensive than this one so I had a good base for comparison.<br /><br />The handle is essentially a solid piece with no adjustable angles and so it\'s critical you have to be at the right angle or the effectiveness goes down very quickly. In fact if you\'re consistently at a suboptimal angle then it will be almost nothing more than a convenient back scratcher.<br /><br />Essentially the housing unit snaps in and is a solid piece that you can push to pull out so it\'s really a fancy plastic tool that you connect into. The housing unit houses what amounts to two side by side three blade heads so that it\'s an extra wide shaving surface with an extra thin lubrication strip.<br /><br />While it does get the job done if you\'ve ever used another brand that has large blades engineered for its use along with a bendable adjustable arm and a lot more reuse from what I can imagine then you\'ll probably be disappointed in this.<br /><br />Overall in comparison I would expect this to retail for about half this price or less so I don\'t really think it\'s a very good value for the money in my opinion.',B0BJV53CYT,AE3RD6NH5YUI7CKMUSXSCAP7V5QA
