1,'This little gadget first and foremost is very difficult to use.  Starting with charging.  It’s difficult to get the plug in.  Once it’s charged you can easily power it on and select one of three settings.  But to actually USE the product you have to keep your fingers on the metal edges.  I did finally discover that contrary to the instructions you can also keep them on the small V at the base…basically you just need to have two fingers on the metal to complete the current loop. (That alone worries me! I have another device that it’s similar and it doesn’t require sending a charge through my body.) Once your fingers are on the base you have to figure out how to move this across your face while keeping your fingers in constant contact.  It is thoroughly awkward! I also found it to be too wide to move along all the surfaces of my face.  It fit okay on my neck but was tough to lay against my face because the curve was greater than the area I was moving over.<br /><br />The settings don’t make sense.  The first one “cleans”.  Sure, whatever…how does a different colored light clean?  The second setting is the one I was interested in.  The IPL setting.  Based on how junky it was I don’t think it’s anything more than a different colored light.  The third setting is suppose to be warm. It was barely perceptibly warm in a couple tiny spots.  Don’t expect the entire surface to warm up.  Again the similar product I have gets really warm is is super soothing.  This one you probably wouldn’t recognize as warm if you didn’t know that’s what it was set too.  And as for the sonic vibration is more of a clattering and rumble. Again does nothing but makes a bunch of weird noises.<br /><br />Lastly the cover does not stay on at all. Not even a tiny bit.  It wasn’t even designed with a lip or groove or tab or anything to realistically expect it would stay attached to a smooth plastic surface.  Save your money and skip this item.',B0BWWBTHP6,AGDQOVGWTV55MLOKGX3YFLGXCZTA
