5,'It\'s been about 2.5 years since we installed soapstone countertops in our kitchen. At first, we left it natural to see how it would age, but switched to Dorado wax because of splotchy darkening and our Kitchen is pretty open.<br /><br />It goes on easy, dries well enough to buff out guickly, and hand buffing leaves a low sheen easily. There\'s no waxy or oily feel once it\'s buffed.<br /><br />It does pick up water marks--as all waxes do. We\'ve learned to wipe surfaces as we work. Also, they easily buff out after cleaning. You also lose the ability to set hot pans directly on the countertop. But that\'s not exactly a ding.<br /><br />We touch up as we go and reapply every 9 to 12 months',B0865GZPZY,AEHZRKMD7KYOOJCSG7WEZLW5BABA
