4,'A few years ago I had cataract surgery that has actually made my night driving worse than better. I\'ve not been able to drive at night and if it rains or snows, I ac\'t see a thing. So when I saw the ad for these night vision glasses I felt they would be worth trying and knew I could probably find these on Amazon. The product quality is quite good and comes in a sturdy case. I gave the glasses a try one night and felt they were helpful. I\'m not certain if they would help me in rain or snow but for driving at night they did seem to settle down all the light trails and stars. I haven\'t tried these yet in city driving where there are more lights and so I am uncertain whether these will help. I have a feeling that with all the added car lights, traffic lights, lights from stores and restaurants that these probably would not help. My gut tells me this because on country roads I still had stars and trailing lights from on-coming cars, but the glasses did turn down the intensity. I would recommend these for others with similar issues.',B00H0DJ664,AFIABPXH5FP3Q7PP3MYK3C6VUZUQ
