5,'I am 10 weeks out of knee surgery (ACL). When I first stood up, my brace slid down to my foot. It never stayed in place, therefore it was more hazardous than helpful. I purchased this brace and, after using it, I was elated! It is a streamline brace that doesn\'t get in the way of your attempt to walk. The aluminum alloy makes it lighter than typical braces and the neoprene grips my leg instead of sliding. My favorite aspect is the STRAP. It gives me a feeling of security, knowing that the brace won\'t slide down. My surgeon and physical therapists are impressed with the design, materials and the addition of the strap. I have had other leg injuries requiring full leg braces. This is the best one I have ever used. As pictured, my leg swells. The velcro makes it easy to loosen the straps while I\'m lying down. To my satisfaction, the velcro has remained very strong despite constant use.',B07NS1RP2F,AH5CO3W3KP2KSAZIQSJLWUQFVEOQ
