5,'Perfect for me.  I am a petite woman with ms, and I love this little scooter!  Being that said, I do not recommend for overweight people as it is a lightweight vehicle.  I am 5\'3&#34; and around 135lb.  I used to ride dirt bikes and three wheelers back in my day (1980\'s) when I was in my twenties, and so the single front wheel does not bother me..it\'s all in how you lean when taking corners, LOL.  This scooter is not made for rough terrain and does great on asphalt, concrete and similar surfaces..Walmart, malls, outdoor venues with solid surfaces like asphalt is the best for this one.  I have not taken it on gravel or dirt so I cannot say if it will do well with that.  I does well on a decent incline, but I am a small/med size woman so that has a lot to do with the performance.  I can pick it up myself and put it in the car...it breaks down easily as I only have so many spoons, I was looking for something that I didn\'t have to disassemble into a million pieces to get it into my trunk..I drive an Altima btw.  Fits perfect!  The main thing for me is the place under the seat to stash a second battery!  For the application of it\'s intention..I highly recommend!',B06XJ9MJYW,AGAIKXHLKMI2XWV62F5PP2OXFBYQ
