5,'I\'ve had the Vulfix 660 brush for a few weeks. It\'s taken a little while to develop the right technique for lathering up but now it is quite easy. The brush is soft and holds a good amount of water to really get and hold the lather. The molded handle is very sturdy and, unlike some of the name-brand plastic handles, much less likely to chip or break. There has been no unpleasant odor and maybe one hair fell out the first day. Since then, no bristles have come loose. I use a chrome brush stand to dry the brush, bristles down, after thoroughly rinsing it - just like caring for a fine paint brush. This is very important.<br /><br />I\'d purchase the Vulfix 660 again (although don\'t expect I\'ll need to for a very long time) and would certainly recommend it.',B0067DHS4U,AFJHZ4PX3HSV4M64OCZO2R7D73JQ
