5,'I used tape on some loose end tiles in a doorway and butted something solid against the tape to prevent leakage before pumping the stuff into the holes I drilled. It worked just fine. Those tiles are now solidly in place. I\'ll be getting to the easier loose tiles next. One tube a day for the next few days should take care of all my loose tiles. Don\'t press down too hard on the tip or it will bend and don\'t pump it in too quickly. Cleaning overflow is easy. I\'d advise repairing cracked grout to prevent unwanted leakage. Great stuff!<br /><br />2 1/2 years after repairing over 40 loose tiles, there is no sign of a single one loosening or sounding hollow. No sign of a crack in repaired grout. The company claims the repair lasts a lifetime and I believe this to be the case.',B009Q946R4,AFTVECFDUZDTJTVIF663AZNG7MDQ
