5,'These foam absorbent adhesive dressings work well to \"suck up\" drainage on most open wounds.  I used different size under an Unna\'s Boot\" in fall of \'19, but my doctor didn\'t want me to continue using it because he wanted Unna\'s Boot to get any positive credit. How mature! I like the 6x6 size, but way too expensive for me. Now I need 1 1/2 -2 of these 4x5 pads to cover 3 remaining leg wounds that are extremely slow to heal. I hope the price stays the same so I can continue with them. They stay on long enough to pick up & wrap leg with Kling/rolled gauze afterwards. Since I\'m disabled, bed rest is mostly my home, so I use ABD pad on back of leg to help protect it from further breakdown while wounds are healing.',B07C64DVSH,AFXVOM24JL7OMMEJEY7HEA7DYH3A
