5,'Glycerin is the key to great lotions. Some deny this because it\'s a petroleum by-product. But so is Vaseline. So is all forms of makeup.<br /><br />I mix my lotion one third glycerin and two-thirds water. It\'s OK that way, but I like the lotion to be thicker than water, so I add any compatible drug compounding base I\'ll buy from a pharmacy. Unibase used to be the best compounding agent, but that\'s been years ago and the new ones are better.<br /><br />Add the essential oil you like the most, mix, and the job is done...for months. (Be careful to date the containers; glycerin has a life span, after which it is no good.)<br /><br />This particular brand of glycerin is very high grade. Read the bottle, and/or the approved methods of grading glycerins. I think you\'ll find this product well worth your money.',B004C7MTLA,AG7E67V3LSFH333SKU4JDWUZ5BAA
