3,'I\'ve been wanting one of these since I first saw them hit the market, and was delighted to get a discount on it.  I tried it for the first time today.  My hair is slightly wavy, mostly because of the gray hair intermixed with my normally straight hair.  I like straight hair, but not plastered to my head.  I am able to add volume to my hair using a straight iron by lifting it up while using, and curling under slightly on the bottom.<br /><br />Maybe the brush will take some getting used to, but my first attempt wasn\'t great.  Even though I used it under my hair to try to give it lift, and tried to give the ends a little curl under, I was unable to get anything but straight, plastered to my head, hair.  However, that\'s better than no styling at all.  So I rate it at 3 stars thinking that it\'ll be good when I\'m in a big hurry, and perhaps I\'ll learn how to better use it.<br /><br />Also, I agree with the people who said there could be more information in the instruction manual.  Perhaps a section on recommended usage ideas for different kinds of hair, or different looks desired.',B01F2ILAWG,AG2QHRLPH3IDWSN4VHC7H72MJERQ
5,'Want your wheels spotless? And don’t want to damage them? Then buy this product. I’ve been in the custom car game for awhile. I’ve never seen such an amazing product. The smell is a little rough. But that’s the only deterrent. Make sure you use when wheels are cool and outdoors. A miracle worker in a bottle. Highly recommend.',B076659PVD,AFYTPM7O5RIMBQFQALIVMLVOYQ7A
5,Perfect!,B008C8T742,AEP3GBS4TPUCVWRRJKNN7I4PR4ZA
5,'Great product. I take a lot of pills, several for pain, several that need to be taken on an empty stomach and a thyroid med that has to be on an empty stomach and apart from any supplements that are metals (calcium, magnesium...). My doctor originally had me taking regular release malate capsules, two twice a day, that had me running to the bathroom. Later, I started pain meds that did the opposite, so I was able to add magnesium back in. Together that made too many large pills all day long. The Jigsaw SRT really helps me fit everything in. I usually take just one tablet once a day, only sometimes twice a day. This way I have time and room to eat between all the dang pills!',B00N7431MU,AFQRP3AIZ6HHK57AZ2OYLCF3HQIA
4,'It\'s no sex panther, but maybe that\'s a good thing. I\'m not entirely sold on the fact that products like these truely work, but for some reason or another this one seemed to work pretty well. It\'s not bad smelling and seemed to give me that caveman edge over everyone else on the club floor. Maybe it\'s in my head, but I feel like this works.',B000OV06V8,AGLN64XLNILQKR6XZBDNO54NVCMA
4,'These heated slippers are so great! They are wonderful to settle back & relax in the warmth they provide<br /><br />But that\'s also where one of their drawbacks becomes apparent. When my slippers arrived I made sure to fully charge their battery packs & then settled down to enjoy their heat. Turning on the TV, I tilted back in my recliner to enjoy the evening. Now, I don\'t know about you, but when I lie back in the recliner I often cross my legs at the ankles. Doing that, the on/off button that is normally on the outside of each foot ends up pressed against the other slipper\'s on/off button. And yes, I didn\'t even notice it until I felt like my toasty toes weren\'t being toasted so much anymore. The slight shifting I\'d done in my chair had turned my \'high\' setting down to \'medium\' on one foot & to \'low\' on the other. It\'s a minor thing, but I wish there was some way to set the on/off button switch so it can\'t accidentally be changed by such a minor bumping.<br /><br />My other minor quibble is with the relative \'run\' time of the batteries. I like toasty feet and at the highest heat setting the instructions say I shouldn\'t really expect more than 2-2½ hours of use. If I\'m in front of the TV for a marathon binge I can certainly spend more than 2½ hours in one evening.<br /><br />Now, with that info, I explored Amazon to see if there were any questions about ordering replacement or supplemental battery packs. No questions, but a search for \'Kamlif battery\' brought up just the 2-pack spare batteries that I was hoping for. As I write this they sell for $26.99. I ordered a set just so I can relax knowing that if/when one set runs down, I can replace them immediately with the back-up set.<br /><br />With those slight drawbacks known, I can wholeheartedly recommend these slippers if you suffer from chronic cold feet.',B0BM518BZZ,AG4PBCM67RSDJMSOUCJ73T2RIKZQ
