2,'It\'s ok.<br /><br />Honestly, this is not what I was expecting or hoping for.  The size is fine.  It\'s states that thes7e are 24cm long up to size 6 shoe, which would be a 7-8 woman\'s shoe when you jump from kids/mens sizing over to woman\'s/<br /><br />I bought this pair more for our 14yo daughter who wears a 6-7 woman\'s shoe, or if she didn\'t like it or ift her, out youngest wears a kids 2, so I knew I oculd cut it down for him.<br /><br />So, really the size is fine.  But, I think MOST poeple looking for a kid\'s insole probably want the small or med and probably want to err more on the smaller side -ordering smaller not bigger in THIS item for kids near the line of 2 sizes.<br /><br />ok, so, I\'m disappointed because it\'s listed as an &#34;Orthtotic Sports Insole Arch and Comfort Support&#34;.  Two works stook out to me when chooising what to buy.  ORTHOTIC and ARCH Support.  My kids all have very flat feet, with ankle pronation and other effects from the lack of internal arch support.  I do try to buy them shoes with support, and like to have inserts to help, especially with shoes that are severly lacking.<br /><br />The Arch support in these insoles is frankly pathetic.  The blue you see in the pucture is what provides the &#34;Arch support&#34; it\'s a very thin, very light plactic that doesvnot hold shape with any reasonalble pressure.<br /><br />The create a real arch support you have to have a firm, relentless plactic that doens\'t give in to pressure, otherwise, why waste plactic there, other than to look like it\'s doing something.<br /><br />I gave them to my daughter to try and she said the insoles are too think, don\'t really add much for her shoes.<br /><br />I do like the grippy material on the bottom - wish other insoles had that.<br /><br />They would work fine in a shoe that is missing it\'s insoles or really only has a flat piece of thin foam - they are better than that.  But, these are NOT an orthotic and do not have any real arch support.  A shame really.<br /><br />I\'m not sure if these will get used at all.  I don\'t think my daughter wants to bother with them, and I won\'t use them for our younger son unless they replace something that provides less support.<br /><br />I received this product at a discount in exchange for an honest review.',B01G8Z1WGQ,AEBNMVVNUOX744HS5FLXWSHQ37UQ
