4,'These things make washing your hair (or your dog\'s fur/skin!) so easy. I\'ll use these forever. They detangle gently when properly used, relieve scalp itchiness or head pressure, and speed up the lather process of washing ones hair.<br /><br />As a per brush, it pulls a lot of shedding fur out and makes scrubbing your dog easy. The rubber spikes massage and pull undercoat out gently when your dog\'s fur is wet.<br /><br />They do eventually tend to get water inside and mold as the pressure from scrubbing your scalp with it pulls the rubber from the plastic and creates a crack for water to seep into the handle, but by then, it\'s normally time for a new one anyway, as the spikes become less firm (like a toothbrush almost) and even discolor over time due to effectivness of scrubbing the scalp.<br /><br />I will say that because of the eventual moisture-inside-the-handle issue, the transparent scrub brushes are the ideal choice. With the opaque ones, you won\'t necessarily be able to see when water is inside.<br /><br />Plastic use could also be reduced... it feels wasteful to get these every 6 months to a year.',B089JYW753,AH7L3OHJZOBDPNNZKVAISF5FYSAA
