3,'I have an eleven year old son named Toby. He\'s a good chap. If I had the means to spoil him I would. Lately his behavior has been quite erratic. He has been picking fights with the elderly, defiantly soiling himself in public, and just last Tuesday was even disruptive at the buffet! I desperately needed some answers and last night I finally got some. I came home from work to find him him sitting on the floor facing the wall. He was rocking back & forth and in tears. He told me that the bananas that I was packing for his lunch were often bruised and sometimes even lacerated! How could I let this happen? If I cannot protect my sons bananas how can I protect him? I know with all the mayhem in the world I can only protect him so much but as a parent I need to keep his optimism intact as long as possible. I cannot send him out into the world bruised! He is not a banana! He is a boy!',B000VY8836,AEDL726G5DH5EBAD7Q5767SLIOBQ
