5,'Love this stuff.  For some bizarre reason, I only get poison oak from my dogs harness, not from his fur.  I discovered this stuff and started using it to wipe down his harness after hikes or walks in areas he goes through poison oak.  It works wonders. He does not like the smell of it, but he suffers through the few minutes of the wipe down and I don’t get poison oak. I had read that it could reduce the duration of the poison oak or even somewhat neutralize it evenafter the blisters started to show on the skin, so  I have also tried it twice and it did definitely help! Great stuff and have given it away and recommended it to many people after hikes.',B01HDTFPC8,AG53VPSFQ2LRIHLUEZOQRHBJYVDQ
