1,'I am sorry that I have to agree with the other one-star reviews. I had the same problem with difficulty loading the pages properly, noisy operation, and frequent (and inevitable) jams. Most of the time, after attempting to turn just one page, one of the turners would get stuck, and it would be jammed. I had to force it back to normal, after which it would just jam again. And this was the second unit I had, since the first wouldn\'t power up right out of the box. The customer service was very kind and helpful, but the product just doesn\'t work well.',B0030DLNS2,AHIRPDADAGN7QCOYK2G6OKSPRWEA
1,'I knew second that I saw the infomercial that the eye would snag the fabric. I lookd to my sister and said, \"If it\'s catching the sewing thread then won\'t it catch the threads of the fabric?\"<br />Thank goodness I didn\'t spend my hard earned money on this junk. I\'m a housekeeper and I was at work and the door handle caught my shirt and made a button come off my uniform. We have mini sewing kits that we give to guests when they ask for them but I didn\'t have one on me. I remembered that a guest had thrown out a sewing kit in a little red box. I had thought they just needed it for a one time fix and kept it on my cart. Now I know why they really threw it out. First thing I noticed when I opened it up was that the needles were thick. For a second I thought they might be spares for a sewing machine. I picked the thinnest one (which still was just as thick as a push pin) and tried to thread it. I couldn\'t get the thread through like a normal needle so I looked closer and realized it was a One Second Needle. I checked the box it came in and saw that one of the plastic inserts had the name there. I decided I would try it out. I tried threading it like they did on tv. You have to yank on the thread in order to get it through the eye. I broke the thread twice before doing it right. When I tried sewing the button back on it confirmed what I had originally thought. It snagged the fabric and not only that but it also left holes it went through because of how thick it was. Needless to say I threw out the needles and kept the rest of the kit. I went and got a real needle and was done in no time.',B004LMWV8M,AGSAJCAEUCW76I6E6FDM62TIBFSQ
