3,'This water flosser is a bit awkward in design, but it does clean teeth well. The build materials are somewhat robust. I already dropped this on the floor by accident, and it still works fine. The replaceable plastic tip did break off with a piece still inside the connecting part, but it was easy to remove and replace. It comes with replaceable tips.<br /><br />The flosser comes with a plastic reservoir to fill with water. There\'s a plastic tube that reaches into it to pump out the water. It holds plenty of water.<br /><br />The spray from the water flosser is powerful. It really blasts away through the crevices and gaps. It takes a little getting used to, and I accidentally sprayed water on the wall. Guess I should be more careful where I aim this thing. It can be a bit awkward trying to turn it on and off. Not a huge issue.<br /><br />You can change the pulse patterns of the spray or leave it on a steady stream. It doesn\'t hurt teeth. However, if you have sensitive teeth, pay special attention to the temp of the water. Personally, I have cold sensitivity, so I use warm water.<br /><br />It\'s not a bad product. It works just fine. However, my issue is with the design. It can be hard to maneuver inside your mouth because of the bulky design. It can fall over easily if there\'s no water in the reservoir, because it\'s a little top heavy. I recommend removing the reservoir after use or store it in an organizer or something.<br /><br />But, yeah, I like this way better than using dental floss.',B0BD3J31NY,AG3X64NX5N2HTSPH5UXJGEMTVQUA
