5,'Luckily, these 300cc were the first i got with my freeze dryer. Thinking most were created alike i bought a few other brands trying to save a few bucks and that was a terrible decision. They seriously dont work NEARLY as good as these! Spend the few extra cents per unit trust me! Some of the other ones were so bad i simply tossed them out. The ones that are ok at best i use in storing food like rice that doesnt really require them, but is not a bad idea so not a totall loss.<br />Oddly enough these 300 cc seemed to work even better than their 500 cc i tested. I used pint jars and put one of each in different jars and these really always seemed to remove the most o2. I will without a doubt always use these, ecspecially for my freeze dried foods. Its not cheap or short process to FD and i dont want to lose 30 dollars over trying to save 5 cents.<br />P..S if you are new to this, I suggest 2 absorbers per 1 gallon bag over the one thats usually suggested ecspecially if your food contains alot of air space like pastas. If you are storing food that has very little and you think you can burp most the air out before sesling one would be fine but again, after all that work im spending the extra few cents to be sure.',B07BWK79ZW,AGX7X3OYOE3DHFBJODE6ZZ3ZQCTA
5,'Just like in the store⭐️',B07WGFHDWV,AFXJL2HSHL22UIFYJAD6AQPNH5RA
5,'I honestly cannot figure out what Voodoo makes these things work... But they are seriously Magic. I have never found a product that is so accurately named, they really do work exactly as advertised. I first learned about them when the company who sold me my spa suggested using them for cleaning scum off the tub surface. I bought them and they were amazing. I used a microfiber cloth and scrubbed , nothing.... picked up a magic eraser and with almost no effort it removed all the filth on surface of the tub. Because it works so well I tried it in my shower, on my sink in the kitchen, even on painted surfaces where the walls were starting to look dingy, unbelievable results. I cannot recommend these things enough, pick up a pack and you\'ll keep two boxes as a reserve forever.',B00BR1FSU8,AEMLBFW5KR3LHIFJLX3UU7AFLFYA
5,'My go-to cloth diaper detergent for both my kids over the last 4 years. Gets everything clean, no stink, no residue. A bag lasts a long time. 2TB a load usually does it. Great to use for other loads of laundry or a good presoak for something. I typically get the classic plain, but the watermelon scent is fun.',B003N0JXSE,AF3HQU7YWRUSK3DOWYYOZBZWZLNA
5,'Turned out great for my daughters birthday party, great quality and easy to assemble',B07CZYTJ93,AFLZG2WUSH4IFMMZT4PYCJNDY64A
5,'Many years ago now, when I went to a chiropractor, he gave these exact gel packs away for free, with his business printed on them. I have squished them, had them in the car, sat on them and they held together. So after many years, it was time for new ones, the old ones still can be used but they are not as plump an more, these are 5 years old. The gel is no longer clear and over time some as seeped out. I have looked and looked for gel packs but never thought to look on Amazon for this brand until the other day when I was using the old one, the light bulb kicked on and I found this 5 pack for a very reasonable price compared to others out there. And they were the product I have been used to. I have Osteoarthritis an am in lots of pain so I have these all over the house, one at the computer, one at my favorite chair, one in my bedroom, one in the refrigerator for a bad pain day. Now, these are very cool just at room temperature, I might add and sometimes they make your lower back sweat. SO what I came up with is a cover for them. I bought 13x13 washcloths here on Amazon, it was a pack of 4. Now you could use 12x12 but the 13x13 is the color and thickness I wanted. SO how do you make the cover? open the washcloth now fold it in half, making sure the fancy edge is up at the top ( if you look at image you can see it) . Now using straight pins pin along the bottom and up the side making sure all is even. I do not have a sewing machine so I sewed these by hand and all on the outside not turning them inside right ,and with needle and thread. I plan to put a button on them with just a thread loop to hold it closed ( good thing I saved old buttons, now if you do this, make sure your button is flat or your back will feel it). When all is said and done, your gel pack will stay in place, and not be sweaty against your back and even if you freeze the pack, the little pouch will protect your skin from the frozen object. This is where you can pick out one or more of those fancy thick facecloths with your favorite theme or color on it. the 13x13 one, you could fit two packs in one if you wanted extra padding. Any way, I hope you have a pain free day and hope you can use my idea with your new gel packs.',B01GSLSNCG,AGZFBBHPFZY5G7BRYZTQ3V7FIP7A
