3,'An herbalist recommended that I purchase an inexpensive ionic foot bath to help with detoxification.  I did some reading, and although I was not convinced that these gadgets do much of anything, I bought one anyway.  I went with this one because it seemed like it was from a reputable company and had a decent price and provided a money back guarantee.  I did notice that Amazon sells a cheaper one that looks exactly like this.  But I went with the slightly more pricey one, just in case.  The unit is easy to use - and you can look up more specific instructions on youtube.  The infra red belt is useless at least for me.  However, it is so obvious that the matter and color is coming from the array.  And the more times you use it, the darker the water becomes because the array becomes more corroded after each use.  I don\'t know.  It DOES work for some people - and that is awesome.  I cannot knock this product, but time will tell.  For me, I continue to use it 1 or 2x a week and hope it will begin to take effect.  If you are looking to detoxify, I would say, go ahead and get the cheaper one sold on Amazon because it seems to be the same product!',B003U4ZKRQ,AES4DDOTLVNBGRC2ZQAOWZ3MPKFA
