1,'I have used these gloves once and i expect them to last a while! They are not super heavy duty and they are not thin. You can get a good feel for what you\'re touching through these. They have a decent grip to them, i normally wash dishes by hand and glass can be slippery when soaped up...these gloves did just as good a job as my hands as far as grip. The brush part is ok, not super firm to get tough caked on bits but for all general cleaning it does the job and certain helps with foaming so you don\'t need gobs of soap. Overall I\'m pretty pleased.<br /><br />UPDATE: 1 glove has a leak... very mysterious, i don\'t wash knives or sharp things wearing the gloves. Very tiny slit in the palm area, almost looks like it could have been product design. I\'ve sent for a replacement, free of charge as long as i return the used ones....<br /><br />UPDATE #2: I have received a replacement pair, and so far so good, free of defects, free of charge as long as I return the used ones....im going to try to reach out to company again, i dont want to return used dish washing gloves, thats gross and i also don\'t want to be charged for another pair....<br /><br />UPDATE #3:(two months post original review) i punctured the replacement pair🤦 my thumbnail went to scratch some crusties. I patched it by melting the slit and set them aside then went to the store and bought a new pair for 3$',B085NM6VY9,AEOOEM25AAXHGPWIUIR3ZWKGRE6A
