4,'One of the things I hate about traveling or camping is that my teeth never feel clean. At home I have an Oral B electric toothbrush. A regular toothbrush just doesn\'t make my teeth feel as clean.<br /><br />This toothbrush comes with a travel case so I ordered it and took it on a recent business trip. I was pleasantly surprised...it seemed to do as good of a job as my Oral B. And I didn\'t have to plug it in. The battery lasted over a few day business trip and a short camping trip.<br /><br />The only downsides are that it comes with a USB charger without a wall plug, and it has different settings but you have to read the guide to know what they are. I didn\'t bring the guide with me. Also the way to turn it off wasn\'t intuitive. I ended up wanting to do a quick brush (it goes for 2 minutes with a pause every 30 seconds). I hit the power button and it kept going so I ended up setting it down while it was running. It took a couple of times before I discovered you can turn it off but you need to hold down the power button.<br /><br />Overall I would give this 4.5 stars.',B07MG4GZWW,AEAWRY7MOKHZBXRZWK4PQQNTP3HA
