4,'[[VIDEOID:abeea0c1b9b80cefba48ac604aadb080]] This set is a great bang for your buck and is excellent for the Wilbarger Protocol. The bristles are soft and flexible to the touch, but when used for brushing, they provide excellent firm tactile feedback and are very soothing.  I appreciate that the bristles kind of nest into each other, just be careful as they can slightly bend out of place.<br /><br />One negative for my needs is the grip. I have hand mobility issues and appreciate the ridges along the hard plastic and lightness of the brushes, but their rectangular shape can be a bit tough on my hypermobile/stiff hand joints.<br /><br />If you experience allodynia flares, soft touches may \"hurt,\" if you\'re using as a stim toy.. Deep pressure brushing doesn\'t trigger sensitivity, however.<br /><br />Overall, I\'m excited to have this new tool to help with sensory regulation!',B09KDL2HV8,AHSA7MBOKD6MNJIL2G2VT4XVTPPA
