4,'It\'s cheap plastic, the hinges, as someone else pointed out, are flimsy, so I used DUCT tape on the hinges: White for one pad holder\'s hinges, red for another, and purple for the third, so I could tell holders apart for \"new pads,\" \"worn pads,\" \"only backups if I\'m desperate pads.\"<br /><br />The holder is hard to open. I have joint problems, no fingernails to help me out, and I have fibromyalgia and another pain syndrome, so I would have liked something easier to deal with; on a particularly bad day, I struggle, and later in the day, let my husband open the holder, put the pads away.<br /><br />If you\'ve got fingernails and duct tape, for the price, go for it. If you don\'t have either and don\'t want the hassle, buy something or Jerry-rig something better.',B089MTYLKH,AEHRXWKBCLI4XVOFWWUWW2WJQS5Q
