5,'This ointment is great for many things.  Sunburn, itching, colds.  It rubs into the skin very well and does not leave a sticky residue behind.  It\'s an old time remedy and most of us know that the old things usually worked well.  This has been used for many many years which is a testament to how good it is.<br /><br />When I was just a little boy (I\'m over 70 now) my mother used this on me for the reasons listed above.  I still use it.  It\'s really great for dry skin and itching.  I also moisten the inside edge of my nose every night before I go to bed.  Helps keep the head clear and it, by keeping the inside of nose moistened, helps prevent colds.  I could not tell you when the last time I ever had a cold.<br /><br />I highly recommend this product.',B01MSD09V5,AFQAHU4RNUFVQCMOUW6BK4P6WVYA
3,'Unlike almost all the other reviewers, I did NOT get a discount/get this for free. This is completely unbiased.<br /><br />This is my first day using it. Took me a few tries to get the trays correctly molded (unlike some other reviewers, I didn\'t throw them away after i messed them up the first time. you can reshape them as much as needed as long as you get them malleable enough). The light was slightly an issue. I opened it up and went to take out the strip that stops the batteries from connecting, but nothing was there. So I messed around with it for almost an hour trying to figure out was wrong. Well... after a trip to Riteaid (which cost $10!!!! FOR TWO CL2025 BATTERIES!!!) I put in the new batteries and it worked fine. So if you LED light doesn\'t have a plastic strip in it and it\'s not working, be ready to take out a second mortgage for two cell batteries. ANYWAYS...<br /><br />There are no instructions for the &#34;remineralizing gel&#34;. As far as I can tell, you do the same thing as with the bleaching gel, except you don\'t use the light and keep it on for 5-10 minutes. Also, the shade chart seems pretty useless. It\'s more of a grayscale chart.<br /><br />As of right now, I\'m leaving it at 3 stars. I\'ll give it a week or two after I\'ve used it multiple times and then I\'ll update with whether or not its effective at whitening. However, I suspect (because that\'s what the gel is made to do) that it\'s going to work fine. We\'ll see.',B00Y5UDC06,AG6PSNUVIU2YC5MAL64RKY2X7V6A
