4,'My favorite masks come from an Etsy seller who makes them with adjustable head cords -- a loose one across the back of the neck, and a tighter one around the back of the head.  They\'re great when you want to take your mask on and off quickly, like passing people on an exercise walk. This cord gives ear-loop masks almost the same convenience though not quite as much comfort behind the ears.  The one negative is that the plastic connectors are tiny and hard to open when you want to attach the cord to a new mask.  I suspect they\'d be nearly impossible for someone with arthritic fingers to use.<br />I\'ve discovered it\'s possible to force each cord through the catch, without trying to open the connector with my fingers.  Like these enough that I bought two more.',B08DTY2DY4,AEAA25EURIHHIK5CB5UMQZ63TNYQ
5,'Best Shoe Horn EVER. Easy extension with a spring at horn to allow for bending so you can actually get your dang shoe on! Grandson uses it and he is only 4 years old!',B00T6NJGAW,AE4CSWTMYLKK5Y7BEDWAR3OSXAGA
5,'To be honest, I was intrigued by the mention of the product being a \"2021 UPGRADED\" version of massage tools.  Nowhere in the product details, or within the product, is any comment on the specific upgrade.  My examination of the massage tools found nothing extraordinary or innovative in the design or construction.<br />There is no enhancement to the gua sha, which does seem a bit thin.  I will note that the massage roller has one feature found on better quality massage rollers.<br />The massage roller includes a metal collar where the metal axle meets the jade roller.  While this is more of a cosmetic affect, it\'s still a nice visual design element.  The jade stone rollers have excellent coloration. The rollers have decent polishing, retaining some natural feel but having a nice shine.  The plastic grommet inserts are present, which facilitates a quiet and smooth rolling behavior.  The inserts, acting as bearings, also protects the jade and the metal axles from erosive interaction.  The massage roller is visually attractive, with good design elements and quality construction.<br />The gua sha, as mentioned before, is a bit thin.  The jade composition has a coloration similar to the jade rollers, perhaps with a bit more lighter shades.  The gua sha also has a decent polish, which retains some natural texture.<br />Priced at slightly under $13, the cost is appropriate for the quality of jade stone and design. Attached are photos to show real world images, with a ruler for size reference.  Most of the photos confirm the rich coloration of the jade elements.<br />While I don\'t really \'see\' the upgraded aspects (unless their previous version didn\'t have the plastic bearings, which would be a low quality product), this is still a very credible massage roller and gua sha set.  I really like the quality and coloration of the jade components.  As such, the set earns a 4.5+ star rating, with a high level recommendation.',B093Y4SZML,AHPGHDFIU3BUB3RQBP56RQQA7W4Q
