3,'Unfortunately I haven\'t been able to give myself a full cut with these because they arrived right after my last haircut.. I have however used the regular scissors for a couple touch ups and I don\'t know if it\'s the adjustment or the scissors but they don\'t seam to cut too great... They push the hair out instead of cutting... I haven\'t tried the thinning shears yet and I\'m excited to because this is why I ordered the set! But like I said, I just had my hair done so I\'m unable to use them for a few more weeks. Hopefully they will work well. Once I try them I will update my review. But for the time being, the regular scissors are not to my liking... I was fortunate enough to receive this item at a discounted rate in exchange for my honest review but that doesn\'t change my true opinion in any way, just an extra bonus!!!',B01FOURXSW,AF4UGJ4NHWE47TVG5BC4DMQEZPHA
5,'I recently purchased a black GE stove and for some reason they left an unpainted (silver) metal piece across the bottom beneath the broiler drawer which was very noticeable from across the room so I painted it with this high heat black paint and it worked great.  Covered in one coat and the silver metal is no longer noticeable.  Would purchase again.',B016TQQ7Y6,AECYPANSBA4CDDEI67OBJ4WBI5HA
5,'This product is magic. My husband was battling for a year with a stye eye. We bought everything possible to get rid of the stye but nothing worked like this product. The tickness is just perfect a little bit goes along the way. We highly highly recommend it.',B06Y4WY962,AGGK7XCW3AYI2ZQGGHEL33B2URLA
5,'I just tried this on my fried eggs and they were phenomenal!! All I did was sprinkle some over top and cooked it right in. Not saying that this the best way to use this powder, but it WAS crazy delicious.<br /><br />I decided to do that after opening the bag and sniffing it first. Broccoli can have a uniquely unpleasant odor anyway—you know what I’m talking about. In a concentrate like this, I figured it would be pretty ripe, so I was shocked when all I could smell was just a really yummy, savory broccoli soup-type aroma.<br /><br />Honestly, I’m not sure who would then decide to blend this with fruit, oh my word no! That’s a personal choice, obviously but this is not going to pair well with sweet smoothie ingredients in my opinion. Gross.<br /><br />Flavor-wise, it’s sooo much better than I expected! I can think of many other ways to use this. The flavor is amazing. And since I heated it up in a pan, of course my whole house smells like broccoli now. But it’s actually still a very yummy smell, not like the big green fart I was expecting.<br /><br />I’m going to get more of this for sure. I think it’s a brilliant way to work tasty, clean, mega-greens into multiple recipes. The only way that was going to work for me is if it tasted good, and this is crazy delicious, so CHECK. Now, I can’t wait to try the spinach too!',B09C7QLB26,AEVLKHGYFJTBXWPJUESJDLOJ65TA
5,'THIS IS MY FAVORITE SCENT I USE IT IN MY PAJAMA DRAWERS AND UNDERWEAR DRAWERS IT MAKES ALL OF MY THINGS SMELL SO NICE AND CLEAN.  I SIMPLY LOVE THE SMELL.',B00CPM2WX4,AEGEZHBYBQPHBMXBHXVUEOPUZODQ
4,'I actually love this product, though I do not use it as intended. After reading the reviews from my fellow curly, kinky-haired girls, I knew this product would not straighten my hair to perfection. If your hair is super curly and thick like mine, you won\'t get the same sleek finish as a traditional straightener. It also does not get the roots of your hair very well since it is kind of bulky. Also, the button placement is awful. I was constantly having to fix the temperature because I kept knocking it down. That being said, this product is great to use this in place of your blow dryer (your hair should be completely dry before you do it, though). It takes significantly less time and effort than working your hair with a brush in one hand and a blow dryer in the other. I have zero upper body strength, so when blow drying I constantly have to take breaks to give myself a rest. It\'s also great for minor touch ups. When I unwrap my hair in the morning, it takes out some of the bends that sometimes happens when you take your hair down. So, if you\'re happy with your blow drying routine and are looking for a product that will get your hair bone straight-- if you\'re hair is naturally curly, thick or kinky-- then this is NOT the product for you. If you\'re interested in something that will supplement your hair straightening process/routine, either blow drying or minor touch ups, then I would recommend this product. When this big zit on my forehead goes away, I may post pictures.',B01775OUCY,AHWX6JCMZU3CVNGMOJG7XB4GUZKA
5,'Will buy again',B010RS8WUY,AHSEJFSNCLPTRKIM7WGPHMXRJQMA
5,'This is helping us save soo much money in ruined outfits and ruined clothes. We have an 8-month-old who was recently taking antibiotics. Which would cause her to have massive diaper blowouts. The other items we tried meant for baby’s just didn’t work. With this its spray let soak and then typically the first wash will get the stain out. If that doesn’t work… Just repeat the steps spray it on again and let it soak. Then the 2nd wash it will come out looking like new again.',B074MQKN4B,AF5I7PRWDSKGIP6I27BSJVCHJR6A
