4,'Purchased these for our 4-year-old who has multiple life-threatening food allergies. They come with quite a few charms and two different bracelet sizes, one for younger kids, one for older. The charms are a little difficult to put on. You have to squeeze the bracelet and the charm and wedge them into place, but this guarantees that they don\'t fall off or get lost. We did have a problem, though, of the charms ripping. My child was pretty careful with her bracelet, however, she never took it off. She wore it swimming, bathing, etc. All but one of the little charms has ripped at the smallest section, which is the part that keeps it attached to the bracelet. We\'ll have to purchase some more, or look at other options.<br /><br />I like that this bracelet is bright, and a conversation starter. People compliment her on it, and she then has the opportunity to discuss her food allergies. It\'s made get-togethers a litle less stressful, because everyone has the visual reminder not to feed her. The medic alert charm comes with the bracelet, another plus.<br /><br />Overall, we\'ve loved the bracelet, and wouldn\'t be in the market for a replacement if the charms were still in tact.',B0058KDN6U,AHGPSVALMQ6652UOFUWSTLSLWH2Q
