1,'This was /almost/ complete waste of $6. Almost only because I /was/ eventually able to trim my nails, so I can\'t justifiably say it was actually a /complete/ waste... but it was pretty darn close.<br /><br />These clippers do not cut. You have to squeeze with all your might, and then it still only leaves an impression and you\'re forced to tear off the rest of the nail. I don\'t have a weak grip, either; these are just /that/ difficult to use. I do not understand all of the positive reviews; sure, the things don\'t slip in your hands... but how many people actually have an issue with that normally? I mean, I don\'t consider myself a nail clipper snob or anything, and I\'ve only ever really used cheap ones from the store, but I have never in my life had as much difficulty clipping my nails as I did when using these clippers. Perhaps all of the positive reviews are just because people received the clippers for free... I don\'t know.<br /><br />Regardless, don\'t waste your money. If it wasn\'t such a hassle to deal with return shipping, you can bet I\'d be getting a full refund. But, at $6, it\'s just not worth it to me. I\'ll eat the loss and grab a better pair from the store next time I\'m there.',B01DVGC6C4,AGKPPEO5XDXXSLUB4QLTHMEIAUDA
5,'My ears often start hurting after about an hour of wearing a mask so these came in handy. They help tighten the mask to prevent any gaps, keep your ears from hurting because they\'re hooked on the knobs instead of the cartilage in your ear, and they\'re super easy to clean!',B08CDQXPDM,AHIJ4KM54YHQOVBWSPPEBZBHXIRQ
