5,'We purchased two other brands of reishi from a retail store in capsules (each around $25-30) but was too anxious to wait.  Both brands of opened capsules tasted like a very dark chocolate = full of fillers.  Continuing my search I found this Real Mushrooms brand who has ALL the information I was looking for including where it\'s sourced from/grown, polysaccharide content, all ingredients, how it was extracted and that it\'s bitter!  All the reviews backing this up are true.  It\'s more expensive, however I\'ve already learned you get what you pay for with reishi.<br /><br />It\'s only been about 4 days taking it daily so I can\'t say if I notice anything yet.  I read vitamin C helps break down the polysaccharides leading to higher absorption, so I mix 1,000mg of real vitamin C from HealthSource with water (do not take abscorbic acid as it\'s linked with arterial plaque, gallstones, who knows what else), take a big sip of the C water, then dump 1/4 tsp reishi directly onto my tongue, then gulp down the rest of the C water to flush the bitterness out of my mouth.  Also found some info that taking it on an empty stomach first thing in the morning (if you can handle it) , plus extra water &#34;helps flush poisons from your system.&#34;  Today I started doing that and my stomach handled it fine and I\'ve felt remarkably calm despite being a normal workday, so there may be something to it!<br /><br />Luckily we were able to return the originally purchased bottles for full refunds and now have an actual source!',B00ZGKA4L4,AENZFYWW7EAABUQEKD7SRFECC3QQ
5,'We are on our way to Maui and I\'m so glad we have our wrap-a-naps. It will make a LONG flight so much more comfortable. I bought them for my whole family a few years ago for Christmas and they were the best purchase I have made in a long time.',B00ZTC56O4,AFLN7NWE3BYWYHAUKFTJ55SCKCFQ
5,'I have bought this for the last couple years but this year I could not find it locally anywhere so checked and OF COURSE Amazon had it.  Until I had found it again this year I had been using the Weiman cleaner that I used on my cooktop. The weiman just did not work well at all on the soot on the fireplace door. Had to rub and rub to get it off. So as soon as the Rutland arrived I tried it out and it was sooooo much better!  Get a paper towel slightly wet and use a couple tablespoons of the creme and rub it in. It will still take some elbow grease so don\'t expect it to come off immediately but you should be able to see it coming off in a few swipes. Use a few more paper towels wetted to remove the filthy scum and polish off to a beautifully clean glass door.  I use the fireplace continually during the winter months as it heats two floors so i clean the door every 2 or 3 days, when the ashes are taken out. Allow the glass to cool a bit before it applying it or it will dry before you can get the soot off.  Stock up!',B01N4NNNMB,AEVUCMIZQSYH3HXOCCMCTLHWHG3Q
