5,'I purchased this night guard after purchasing and returning a different night guard which I realized, upon its arrival, was meant to cover my top and bottom teeth.  I\'ve used a night guard for about twenty years and I knew there was no way I could stand that.  I have used the SmartGuard Elite for a week now and I am very happy with it.  The molding process was easy (you definitely need to use a fork or a wooden skewer to hold the guard WHERE INDICATED when you place it in the water... the guard will melt to tongs or other devices) and the fit is snug and comfortable.  There has been no &#34;break in period&#34; to get used to the guard.  The guard\'s width is small (it really only covers the front 6-8 top teeth) but it is thick and sturdy, yet comfortable.  My previous two night guards were purchased from my dentists.  I\'d tried an over the counter version in between those but I was not happy with it at all.  I am very happy with the SmartGuard Elite, though, and will continue to use it as a much cheaper and even more comfortable alternative to the version available from the dentist.  The function and comfortable of the SmartGuard Elite is the same or better than the last one I got from my dentist.  Very satisfied with this purchase.',B00O59UTBW,AHWB6WWAZ4JTU3DVQYW4WO3O4Q6Q
