5,'I am currently using this toothpaste exclusively, and I really like it.<br />Before, due to many and painful sensitive \"spots\", I was pretty much confined to Sensodyne and similar products. Also, since I am a moderate coffee and tea drinker, I was also looking for something that can help remove the stains without causing excruciating pain, like the common over-the-counter whitening products do when you have sensitive teeth.<br />I am also nearly 60, so the days of pearly whites are sadly gone, and the teeth need all the help they can get (without spending ridiculously high amounts on veneers) to get remineralized the most natural and affordable way I can find.<br /><br />After doing some reading on the product, and many, many reviews from all over the web, I purchased this toothpaste.<br />I have put it to immediate use, usually three times per day after meals and, after about three weeks, I can already see some subtle results. Many discolorations are becoming much less visible, and my teeth actually look and feel clean. Best of all, the plaque is gone, and I no longer need the customary twice-yearly dental cleaning!<br />Even my dentist made a remark that my \"teeth are being taken excellent care of\". I mentioned the Apagard toothpaste, and he was very impressed with it.<br /><br />Since then, I have bought three more tubes of this wonderful toothpaste, and keep one at work so I can brush after lunch. Apagard is expensive but, I believe, it is money well spent. Peanuts, comparing to the dentist\' fees.',B0157NB0WQ,AHIIQ4K4FWNNEWPPGNVZVK7UFKHA
