4,'I\'ve owned a Withings scale for years, but I lost it in a move, and bought this one as a replacement because it cost significantly less. I had a little trouble setting the scale up, but once set up it\'s working well and I\'m very happy with it.<br /><br />I\'d give it five stars if it had better setup instructions/process. The main point of confusion is setting it up for multiple family members, which it supports, but the process is not a part of the initial setup and the option to add users is well hidden in the UI. It\'s a bit complex as well - you have to email an invitation to the person, then they read their email, accept the invitation, and set up a fitbit account and link the scale to it. Which is a lot to go through to see my family\'s weights tracked. With the Withings I see all of the measurements in a single graph, and I can simply set the names of the people in the software.<br /><br />Still, now that it\'s set up, it works great.',B0077L8YFI,AFAVMC2AZS6OC5DXVQSOZF426DFQ
4,'I like these inserts enough but I probably won\'t buy them again. They\'re thinner than the microfiber inserts but not quite as thin as the hemp ones. However, they feel weird and kind of slinky if that makes sense? Almost like a slinky terrycloth towel. Also they don\'t seem to be as absorbent as the hemp ones. I\'m glad I tried these and I definitely use them, but I wouldn\'t buy them again.',B01H7I48XC,AHUFS2NI3BAUBDN2GV2YZZ2DT4QA
