5,'I have a rare form of pustular psoriosis on the bottoms of my feet.  They get tons of blisters on them every day and can be quite painful!  I was using a regular non-woven retention tape after putting medications and creams and such, and the other tapes, though good tapes in general, did not keep the medication and creams next to my skin and they were very sticky and irritated my fragile skin, and just were not working as I would like, but did not know there was a different choice.... until I was reading an article about manuka honey on my feet for my very hard to treat problem, and to use this tape... OMG!!!  It adheres, but does not \'stick\' if that makes sense... it stays in place, does not stick to my socks, and the silicone in it holds the honey on my skin, forcing it to absorb completely.... AND, it does not hurt or irritate my skin.  Super easy to remove.  The combination of this tape and the honey has made a drastic difference in my feet.... no pain, scales and blisters going down, no irritation... just wonderful!<br />AND... yesterday, my poor pup, a black lab named Jed, injured the pad of one of his back legs.... I did not want to put anything on it that would hurt to remove with his fur and all.... so.... I used a small gauze pad with medicine and then used THIS TAPE to hold it in place.  It is not elastic, so does not get too tight... it simply holds it in place, while keeping out dirt and such.... and comes off like a dream when changing dressings! A miracle tape for pets too!  Win Win!',B07C9YR7GT,AG4VJBAQUATLEJSH3BOLH545RGXQ
