5,'I\'ve tried various calcium tablets, I want to gag. I\'ve tried the chewable soft-candy like calcium from two different vendors, and they are sickly sweet (both vanilla and chocolate). Plus, I don\'t like to have to brush my teeth just because I took my calcium. Then I heard about calcium in powder form. I found a website where the person took pictures as they opened their packets and tasted it and said there was no taste. So I thought great! And bought the canister version.<br /><br />I\'m loving this! At first I put it in my water, I drink a lot of water throughout the day. But it does settle to the bottom if you don\'t drink it right away, so you have to stir it before every drink. So today I decided to just use a smaller glass and chug it as others have suggested. That gets it over and done with and is much less painless than taking tablets!<br /><br />There is a little red scoop in the canister, so use a spoon to dig down into the canister to find it.',B009R2IJLE,AH2KVUMX4T5QXLUT5CCTVYRTAHKA
