5,'I\'ve bought this before, loved the taste, and so have re-ordered it (most recently from Amazon). It\'s no coincidence that Cod Liver Oil has been historically used as a &#34;get well&#34; cure. As with most fish oils, it has high levels of the good omega-3 fatty acids, eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA) and docosahexaenoic acid (DHA). But what sets it apart is that it has higher levels of the natural vitamins A and D (D-3).<br /><br />I love to sprinke this on salads since it adds a lemony zest to the salad flavor (and oils make the nutrients of salad vegetables more bio-available).',B001LF39RO,AH4ECXS47DMST7ANISCX3WH3DY4A
5,'I was amazed by the reviews, so I purchased a bottle!  (crazy shipping cost, but oh well)<br />I\'ve used this product about 11 times now, and I like the results so far!<br />My pimples aren\'t so out of control, and I definitely see more of a smooth & toned complexion.  The acne marks are slightly fading as well.<br />My purchase also came with a free collagen facial cleansing gel.  Love it!  My face actually feels soft and moisturized as I\'m washing/rinsing.  That NEVER happens!  It\'s such a nice feeling.<br /><br />Back to the prep skin refresher.<br />Once applied, I did not feel any sort of burning, but sometimes there is a bit of an itchy feeling.  Goes away once you smooth on a moisturizer, so it\'s no big deal.<br />Anyway, I am recovering from a horrible, horrible breakout and I feel more confident in my skin after using these 2 gems.<br />I will continue to buy (even though they\'re a tad expensive, but I can see why!)<br /><br />Thanks & best of luck!',B000VEMWB0,AFMGWKLPQN3JGIA4VCRPHLZ2DTCA
