5,'This was my first time trying MATCHA Green Tea.  I enjoyed it.  The instructions say to stir it into hot water, which I\'m assuming is necessary in order to best mix-in the product with the water.  It\'s a very fine powder that mixes and dissolves easily.  However, I liked it even better over ice and plan to try it with a little milk next time, in order to give it a creamier texture.  It has a slightly sweet taste, but there are only 1.5 grams of sugar alcohols.  It has a little bit of fruit taste, but mainly tastes like cinnamon.  It\'s too soon to say if it will improve my sleep and some of the other health benefits that are advertised (in general) for MATCHA Green Tea.  But the nice taste is off to a good start and I will buy again if I also see sleep/health improvements.<br /><br />My only nitpick is the instructions could be better.  It says to use one &#34;scoop&#34; into 6-8 oz. of water.  A &#34;scoop&#34; is not included in the packaging.  There is no such measurement as a &#34;scoop&#34;, so that is just a really pointless instruction.  Apparently a serving is 7.8 grams, so I assumed that is how much to use.  I don\'t know about you all, but my kitchen measurements are in teaspoons and tablespoons.  I don\'t think many residential kitchens use grams.  So that was also annoying.  I had to look it up online, in order to get an idea of the suggested amount to use.  It\'s about 1.5 teaspoons or about .5 a tablespoon.  I used half of a soup spoon and that seemed about right for my taste.',B079SXYFQ1,AF6MDCNZG7M4G4PUKBXFAELYQSGA
