5,'I\'ve been building PCs for over 20 years now and I\'ve always used either rubbing alcohol or denatured alcohol to clean thermal paste from my heatsinks and CPUs. Arctic Clean works much better than any alcohol solvents I\'ve tried.<br /><br />You just put a few drops of the solvent on the grease and let it sit for a minute. It completely dissovles the grease and lets you easily wipe it up. No smearing at all.<br /><br />Once you\'ve removed the existing paste just put a couple drops of the purifier on and wipe it clean. The purifier is almost like a thicker version of rubbing alchol. It dries quickly and doesn\'t run all over the place after being applied.<br /><br />I\'m disappointed I waited this long to try this stuff, it\'s defintely worth the money if you\'re going to be cleaning up thermal paste.',B001JYQ9TM,AGX6PGYBLKJUJ6H7ORED4FIQ6H6A
