4,'I bought this baby wipe dispenser to use for Clorox or other disinfecting wipes. I despise the tall, cylindrical containers that disinfecting wipes comes in because inevitably, after I pull out one wipe, even though I stick the end corner in the little grabber thingy at the top, the wipe falls back inside the container. Every single time which means I have to pull the top off, reach inside and reconnect the end of the wipe to the grabber thingy. May sound like a small problem but it annoys the heck out of me. So now I purchase my Clorox or Lysol wipes in the flat packs, such as the ones baby wipes come in. I cut the pack open on the side and just transfer all the wipes in at once. Couldn’t be easier. The bottom part of the top of the lid has some kind of gasket/seal that keeps it tightly closed. I would have given this item 5 stars had it not been for the top part which you lift open to access the wipes. To me, it could close just a smidge tighter but maybe it was just a fluke with my particular one. I put a huge, heavy  book on top for about a week and it seems to close fine now. I’ve been using the wipes for a few weeks now and each one is perfect, not the least bit dried out. And most importantly to me, EVERY SINGLE WIPE comes out perfectly - one at a time, no rips or tears and not attached to the one below it so you don’t have to tuck the bottom one back in. So be it for baby wipes or disinfecting wipes, I really recommend this product.',B098QBFW5Q,AFZ62HIXJPINFNPHWFW3EWY7G67A
4,'These are your basic pastry /  jewelry / take home box for light weight or delicate gifts.  These are not designed to store heavy items in them, if you do put something with any noticeable weight in them you will need to support the bottoms at all times or the box may break open.  Decent size and easy to put together.  Overall, great to keep on hand for quick gifts.',B083BKHC3Z,AEOK4TQIKGO23SJKZ6PW4FETNNDA_1
5,'I\'ve been trying more natural and environmentally friendly cleaners lately. This is by far the best dish detergent I have found. Everything gets very clean and the glasses are shiny. If you have a lot of VERY dirty pots and pans (which I regularly do) you may need to use a traditional oil detergent, unless you pre-rinse/wash (which some studies say is worse for the planet as you double your water waste). For me, still using my old cleaner occasionally is fine, I\'m still reducing my oil based detergent use by 90\%. It\'s overall a win.',B07Z4DW3YT,AFL6IDEKVMRINVJQDMHFNZ4GMI3A
4,'This was fairly easy to assemble, you just have to be cautious with the valves as not to puncture the balloon. My “S” came with a small hole in it but I was still able to manipulate it thankfully. The cactus is a bit frustrating as it has no place to tie a string. Would be better with helium.<br />I attached it to our wall with glue dots.',B07FCZS9XQ,AFLSUSCMULQQQM7AYXDXI2NPRH2A
