4,'I\'ve been using this in our laundry room, where the cat box is, for about 2 months. It has definitely reduced the odor in that room (which is 8 x 6 feet). I also put this in our two-car garage for a couple of days, and it did noticeably reduce the smell in there as well.<br /><br />As others have mentioned, the Germ Guardian is not at all \"whisper quiet\". I suppose it depends what level of noise you are used to, but we live in the country where it is generally silent, and I definitely notice the hum of this. I do not mind it running in the laundry room, but I would not be able to sleep in the same room with it.<br /><br />As for reducing the spread of colds... I wish it worked, but so far in my house it has not. A visitor brought a cold over Christmas and this did not keep us from getting sick. Of course, it was only running in the laundry/cat room. Our house is 1600 square feet, so to clean that much air we would probably need at least six of these. I do not like this enough to buy six of them.<br /><br />Compared to the price and features of other air sanitizers, this is worth a try.',B000G2BESO,AGAPG2MY2AS33WMY4RKGXEOU6RAQ
5,'Quality made unit, the top is adjustable, and it keeps out the noise and conversations on the other side of the door. (I know this; my doctor has one outside his conference room.) This thing is built like it should last for years! I gave it 5-stars because it does what it says, and looks like it should keep on doing it. A little expensive, but over any significant span of years, the cost is relatively miniscule.',B000LQI2S0,AF735G5CSCZPCXWU2RXGH7FXD2RQ
