2,'I purchased this after checking out some videos on youtube of people successfully removing tonsil stones using this product. Unfortunately, whether that was because of the magic of film editing, a different product being used, or someone with better eye-hand coordination skills, I did not fund much success. While this is a good product in theory, I found that this particular model had a tip that was slightly too sharp, being shaped more like a  tiny cup instead of a rounded ball shape I thought I was getting when I looked at the pictures. So when I tried out some probing with my fancy new upgrade from using qtips I ended piercing one of my tonsils when applying a fraction more than slight pressure and actually ended up getting the tonsil stone I was originally aiming for with my tried and trusted supply of qtips after that. I attempted several more probings with similar results. Good in theory, could use some changes to the design. Additionally, the LED light ended up not being as bright as I was led to believe, something that could have been overlooked assuming I didn\'t stab myself every time I used this product.',B00V54LR5C,AFCXTHNZWIKDRPBMEJF5B4ZEYJDA
