5,'This mini pump is great for those times your baby stops eating before the milk runs out. This is smaller than other wearables. And this pump is great if you\'re not producing a lot of milk or if you just need to pump any left over milk. It does seem a bit loud, but it does work well. It\'s just as discrete as other wearables. But the design is definitely different. This has a max fill of 4oz., while most wearables max at 8oz. The instructions are clear and easy to understand, though the English version is at the end of the manual. It does have a lot of parts and that does mean it takes longer to clean, but it\'s still easy to clean. Charges in decent amount of time and charge lasts through multiple pumping\'s. Does not come with a block for charging cord. The duckbill is not in the basin like most wearables, and there haven\'t been any backflow issues. This has 8 levels and 3 modes for pumping. Not overly strong suction. Automatically shuts off after 8 hours. Includes 3 different size flange inserts, so that\'s 4 different sizes in total. So that\'s a 20mm, 24mm, 27mm, and without a flange insert, it\'s 28mm. This pump also includes an extra duckbill.',B0B4FT4H7T,AHVEKNHP5YYEYVLWQSPBDLE2GUYQ
