5,'This is a great walker.  I bought two about 5 years ago from Gold Violin, because I was anticipating shoulder replacement surgery and needed a walker I could use with just one arm.  I cancelled the surgery and didn\'t start using this walker until recently, when my mobility issues became extremely  challenging and I kept falling. (My triangular wheeled walkers became dangerous because I would tip over.) By being able to brake with only one hand I\'m  able to reach out for things with my other hand because I can brake all four wheels simultaneously.  I have one of these walkers on the main floor of the house and the other on the second floor because my legs now are almost totally paralyzed and I cannot take a single step independently. I wanted to buy another walker so there would always be a &#34;spare&#34;.  Without this walker I probably would have completely lost my ability to live alone and would be in a nursing home.  I couldn\'t find the walker or anything similar in any U.S. store but finally was able to track down the manufacturer in Sweden.  It would cost $357 for the walker and $280 for shipping, for a total of $639, which is lower than the Amazon price. I wish that Amazon could lower the price because I absolutely would buy this walker again.',B018OSLI0U,AGLVUS63RRAM2X4PIMSBPBTTUJRA
