5,'Our doctor put our very bow-legged son on vitamin D drops with the instructions to give it to him with a fatty food. I found it difficult to coordinate the drops with fats, so I switched to this cod liver oil. Within a couple of months, his legs have straightened out. What is more, he loves the stuff: he always wants another spoonful! As a side note, people regularly comment that \"he has such great skin color\". I suspect it may have to do with the D and A in his cod liver oil as we, his parents do not share his great skin tone and color. We highly recommend this for children and we intend to give it to our next child instead of the D drops.',B001LF39RO,AFW7GN6XIUMNKX7MOQHT3P5RMPFA
5,'I cloth diapered my older daughter (now 8 years old) in Bumgenius diapers, and now with baby #2 (born January 2016), I\'m doing the same. I\'ve tried a number of different brands with both girls, and Bumgenius are hands down the best. They\'re very easy to use, versatile (you can add extra absorbency when needed, such as at night), they are the trimmest cloth diapers that I\'ve ever used, and come in some very cute prints! The Audrey print in particular is one of the most adorable that I\'ve seen. I used all hook-and-loop (&#34;velcro&#34;) diapers with my older daughter, so I was a bit disappointed to see that Bumgenius is no longer offering hook-and-loop (except in the neworn size), but I\'ve gotten used to the snaps. For me, it\'s not that I find snaps particularly &#34;difficult,&#34; but it\'s more about sizing it perfectly; though that may be more about my Type A personality than anything! I\'m very particular about symmetry, so I like to use the same snap setting on the right as on the left, so if the diaper needs to be adjusted up or down just enough so that I only need to go the the next snap setting on ONE side, it bugs me that they\'re not symmetrical! Again, more a personal problem than a functional one! If I had one suggestion, it would be to place the snaps a little closer together so that the diaper can be adjusted in smaller increments (and that complaint really isn\'t a big deal, and not enough to warrant losing a star!) I highly recommend Bumgenius pocket diapers to anyone.<br />Pros:<br />•Easy to use<br />•Trim<br />•Adjustable Absorbency<br />•Cute Prints<br />•Superb construction<br /><br />Cons:<br />•Company no longer offers hook-and-loop option<br />•Snaps could be positioned closer together so that size could be adjusted in smaller increments',B0193VHP3Q,AHHFVJHD4M3BTUQQBCHYNA4ULBFA
