4,'My mom introduced me to a much earlier version of this “diamond” nail file a million years ago. One side was a bit coarse “for shaping,” and the other was very fine, “for smoothing.” I used to have half a dozen of them for different locations in my house (cuz you never know when you’ll break a nail!) — bathroom, bedroom, kitchen, purse, car… and they lasted forever. Until I lost them all.<br /><br />This is the closest I could find as a replacement. It’s okay, but I can’t discern a difference in “grit” on the two sides, even though they claim it’s double-sided. And unlike the old version, neither side is labeled. So not great. Still, better than an old-school, cardboard-and-sandpaper emery board.',B009W1RL2I,AFY43XSS4AATW6QBXB5CLXB35FCA
