5,'Bought this to replace the batteries in my HX6250-09. For the last few months it has only been making it to the 3rd quarter of the brushing interval before stopping with the low battery alert. Took it apart and put this battery in, let it charge up, and the toothbrush is working as good as new!<br /><br />Be aware that the battery tabs are tiny and replacing the assembly does require a tiny bit of soldering. It only took me about 10 minutes for the whole process though.<br /><br />Highly recommend if your otherwise perfectly fine Sonicare is reaching end of life due to the battery. Would also recommend taking the toothbrush apart and checking the battery type before ordering - some of the models are lithium ion batteries. Mine was a NIMH so this part was a perfect replacement.',B06Y2KD2Y6,AHEAL4CSHDHCJ7IBOSDW5SK6TPCA
